\par\par \b \uc2 Linkers From Germany, France In Same Week Unusual-Citi- -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,723 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2014\par 08:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0655 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] It is quite unusual for both Germany and France to be active with an inflation-linked government bond auction the same week, says Citi ahead of Germany's EUR1 billion tap of the 0.10% April 2023-dated inflation-linked Bund Tuesday. The German linker, according to Citi strategists, offers little value versus its peer despite a roughly 10 basis points rise in real yields since the auction was announced Thursday. Despite the rise in the yield, the German linker is expensive versus peers cross-country as the coming auction will bring its outstanding volume to EUR16 billion, which is higher than EUR15 billion, which was previously assumed to be an implicit ceiling. Hence, the bond is unlikely to be often reopened in the future, and its price won't face supply pressure. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0654 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The description of the eurozone in the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2 's semiannual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  report, which may come out later this week, will likely provide important material for the future direction of exchange rates, says Daisuke Karakama, chief market economist at \uc2 Mizuho Bank\uc2 . The JPY has every reason to weaken, given Japan's trade deficit for three straight years, he says. But on a theoretical basis the EUR shouldn't be declining given that the region has the world's biggest current account surplus. It's only natural for the U.S to think that demand should be stimulated through fiscal action instead of the zone just relying on holding down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he says. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0649 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Australia's equities market rebounded on a rally in mining stocks spurred by a jump in the iron-ore price. The spot price for the steelmaking commodity climbed 4% on Monday. The S&P/ASX 200 ended up 1% at 5207.4, having initially begun the day in the red to build on Monday's close at a fresh eight-month low. Iron-ore producers Fortescue (FMG.AU) climbed 5.5%, Atlas Iron (AGO.AU) surged 15% and Mount Gibson (MGX.AU) rocketed 18%. \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton\f28 \uc2 \f2  (BHP.AU) added 2.6% and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto\f28 \uc2 \f2  (RIO.AU) put on 4.1%. Still, some question whether the recovery has legs. "Given the recent choppy trade we've been seeing and the fact nothing has fundamentally changed since yesterday's losses, we are just as likely to open with red on the screens again tomorrow as traders sell into strength," says Stan Shamu, market strategist at IG. (robb.stewart@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @RobbMStewart) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0639 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]-SEB thinks EUR/HUF will strengthen as far as 308 in what's left of the year, before the forint gets some strength back, possibly as a result of easier monetary policy from the ECB. That could take the euro down to 303 over the next twelve months, the bank says. SEB also thinks Hungarian inflation has probably bottomed out, and that recovery has taken hold, although policy tightening could yet be some way off. EUR/HUF is now 305.92. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0636 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Capital flight from China "could be an outcome" of the Hong Kong-Shanghai stock connect program that is set to allow investors in Hong Kong and Shanghai to buy up shares in each other's stock markets, says Ewen Cameron Watt, BlackRock Investment Institute's chief investment strategist. While many analysts predict that more money will flow from Hong Kong to Shanghai than vice versa, Watt doesn't rule out the reverse happening. He explains that China's huge appetite for gold has already indicated that local mainland investors are eager for ways to diversify their assets. If a significant amount of money rushes from Shanghai to Hong Kong, Watt says that would be in effect a "de facto deregulation" of China's capital account. (chao.deng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0633 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Philippines shouldn't make sending medical workers to Ebola-stricken countries its priority, a former health secretary says, rejecting a proposal by the government to send health personnel to West African countries. Dr Jaime Galvez-Tan, who served as health chief under former President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fidel Ramos\f28 \uc2 \f2 , says the government's "priority should be to safeguard the country's borders against the entry of the Ebola virus given that many Filipino travelers and overseas workers come from Africa." He says that, while the Philippines remains Ebola-free, the country needs its own professionals to attend to its citizens' health needs. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Enrique Ona\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the current health secretary, has said the Philippines is considering a request by the U.S. and U.K. for the Southeast Asian country to help fill the gap health personnel in West African countries. The current Ebola outbreak has killed more than 3,800 people, mostly in Guinea, Liberia and Sierra Leone, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Health Organization\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \uc2 \f2 World Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the two-year cost to West Africa of the Ebola epidemic--if it spreads in large scale to the big economies in the region--could hit $32.6 billion by the end of 2015. (Josephine.cuneta@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0629 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--UK CPI is expected to have risen 1.4% y/y in September, from 1.5% in August, according to analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 , "supporting the market view that the first BoE rate hike will not occur until August 2015." \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2  however continues to see merit in an earlier BoE rate hike given its belief that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continues to underestimate the acceleration of wages, as portrayed by survey measures. UK CPI is released at 0830 GMT. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0620 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently signed an expanded bilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap agreement with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , providing it with additional ammunition to deal with future financial shocks. The new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap doubles the amount the Philippines can borrow from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  to $12 billion. Japan can borrow $500 million from the Philippines. Japan has similar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap deals with other countries in Southeast Asia as part of regional efforts to build a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  firewall to minimize the effects of a future financial crisis, and Japan's own efforts to counter China's growing influence in the region. Southeast Asia was the ground zero of the 1997-1998 Asian financial crisis. (cris.larano@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0619 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/INR began Tuesday on a weak footing after an overnight drop in the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index, but has since rebounded to an intraday high of 61.10. The daily USD/INR chart suggests the pair is still in a consolidation phase of 60.92-61.55 demarcated by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1). Indian state-owned banks were said to have been buying U.S. dollars in the spot market, according to an offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader, likely for funding of energy deals. India relies heavily on imported fuel even though it is an oil exporter itself. Crude oil prices have recently fallen to four-year lows, possibly creating an opportunity for increased stockpiling of oil supplies. USD/INR is now 61.13 from its Monday close of 61.00. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0611 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Taiwan shares end 0.7% higher at 8768.39, as some heavyweights rebound modestly on the back of buying by government-backed funds. First Capital says concerns over global economic growth and lingering food scandals will continue to keep the Taiex trading in a lower range of 8508-9000 in the near term. TSMC (2330.TW) closes up 0.4% at NT$121.00, Hon Hai (2317.TW) gains 0.2% to NT$96.00 while Catcher Technology (2474.TW) adds 2.1% to NT$271.00. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wei Chuan Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1201.TW), a unit of Ting Hsin that used substandard oil in some of its lard-based products, falls by 7% (the maximum allowable daily limit) for the second straight session to NT$27.25. (aries.poon@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0559 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Philippine President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Benigno Aquino\f28 \uc2 \f2  might soon get his wish for emergency powers from congress to deal with the looming power crisis. The Department of Energy estimates the main island of Luzon, which accounts for more than half of the country's gross domestic product, may face up to 13 weeks of power outages in the summer of 2015. Emergency powers for Aquino would allow the government to lease additional electricity capacity, mainly mobile diesel generators, to fill the supply gap. Philippine laws has left power generation in the hands of the private sector, but the government is allowed to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in cases of emergency. Economic growth in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , one of the fastest in Asia in recent years despite having one of the region's most expensive electricity rates, could stall in the event of severe power shortages and new investment may be delayed, if not cancelled. (Josephine.cuneta@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0549 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY managed to gain on dip buying in Asian trade, but may suffer a setback if U.S. stocks tumble again and \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  prices increase, says Toshihiko Sakai, senior manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and financial products trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi UFJ Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Banking. The key is "how much the market has factored into the risk from the U.S. stocks decline," says Mr. Sakai, adding that recent declines in the 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield to below 2.3% show "we are now coming to the level to think about how far we can go ahead with buying [the dollar] from this point." The USD/JPY is now at Y107.08 after hitting one-month low of 106.76. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 14, 2014 02:55 ET (06:55 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141014eaae000jj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
