\par\par \b \uc2 UK CPI Expected to Weaken - \uc2 Barclays\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2014\par 08:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0629 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--UK CPI is expected to have risen 1.4% y/y in September, from 1.5% in August, according to analysts at \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , "supporting the market view that the first BoE rate hike will not occur until August 2015." \uc2 Barclays\uc2  however continues to see merit in an earlier BoE rate hike given its belief that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to underestimate the acceleration of wages, as portrayed by survey measures. UK CPI is released at 0830 GMT. (nick.cawley@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0620 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \uc2 Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  recently signed an expanded bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap agreement with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , providing it with additional ammunition to deal with future financial shocks. The new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap doubles the amount the Philippines can borrow from the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to $12 billion. Japan can borrow $500 million from the Philippines. Japan has similar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap deals with other countries in Southeast Asia as part of regional efforts to build a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firewall to minimize the effects of a future financial crisis, and Japan's own efforts to counter China's growing influence in the region. Southeast Asia was the ground zero of the 1997-1998 Asian financial crisis. (cris.larano@dowjones.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: PJK \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0619 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/INR began Tuesday on a weak footing after an overnight drop in the benchmark ICE U.S. dollar index, but has since rebounded to an intraday high of 61.10. The daily USD/INR chart suggests the pair is still in a consolidation phase of 60.92-61.55 demarcated by the lower and upper Bollinger bands (standard deviation 1). Indian state-owned banks were said to have been buying U.S. dollars in the spot market, according to an offshore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader, likely for funding of energy deals. India relies heavily on imported fuel even though it is an oil exporter itself. Crude oil prices have recently fallen to four-year lows, possibly creating an opportunity for increased stockpiling of oil supplies. USD/INR is now 61.13 from its Monday close of 61.00. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0611 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Taiwan shares end 0.7% higher at 8768.39, as some heavyweights rebound modestly on the back of buying by government-backed funds. First Capital says concerns over global economic growth and lingering food scandals will continue to keep the Taiex trading in a lower range of 8508-9000 in the near term. TSMC (2330.TW) closes up 0.4% at NT$121.00, Hon Hai (2317.TW) gains 0.2% to NT$96.00 while Catcher Technology (2474.TW) adds 2.1% to NT$271.00. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wei Chuan Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1201.TW), a unit of Ting Hsin that used substandard oil in some of its lard-based products, falls by 7% (the maximum allowable daily limit) for the second straight session to NT$27.25. (aries.poon@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0559 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Philippine President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Benigno Aquino\f28 \uc2 \f2  might soon get his wish for emergency powers from congress to deal with the looming power crisis. The Department of Energy estimates the main island of Luzon, which accounts for more than half of the country's gross domestic product, may face up to 13 weeks of power outages in the summer of 2015. Emergency powers for Aquino would allow the government to lease additional electricity capacity, mainly mobile diesel generators, to fill the supply gap. Philippine laws has left power generation in the hands of the private sector, but the government is allowed to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in cases of emergency. Economic growth in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , one of the fastest in Asia in recent years despite having one of the region's most expensive electricity rates, could stall in the event of severe power shortages and new investment may be delayed, if not cancelled. (Josephine.cuneta@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0549 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/JPY managed to gain on dip buying in Asian trade, but may suffer a setback if U.S. stocks tumble again and \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  prices increase, says Toshihiko Sakai, senior manager of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and financial products trading at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsubishi UFJ Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Banking. The key is "how much the market has factored into the risk from the U.S. stocks decline," says Mr. Sakai, adding that recent declines in the 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield to below 2.3% show "we are now coming to the level to think about how far we can go ahead with buying [the dollar] from this point." The USD/JPY is now at Y107.08 after hitting one-month low of 106.76. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0547 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A respite from risk aversion in stocks is helping the Indonesia rupiah to stage a small rebound. USD/IDR has slipped to 12,195 from its Monday close of 12,215 as Jakarta stocks rise 0.2%. The bullish technical bias for USD/IDR could be extinguished on a Tuesday close below 12,210. If this chart support breaks, the rupiah could rally to the 20-day Bollinger mid line at 12,100. But domestic political woes may deter further gains. Political rivals are trying to link president-elect Joko Widodo to corruption charges in an attempt to derail his October inauguration. A polically-motivated delay of economic reforms might be a strong negative factor for the rupiah if skittish foreign investors decide to trim their exposure to Indonesia. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor SXS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0425 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Singapore's third quarter economic data shows strength, but is still fundamentally tied to the fortunes of global growth, Capital Economics says. "As long as the recovery in the global economy does not falter, Singapore's growth should pick up over coming quarters," the research house writes. "Despite recent concerns the global recovery may already be faltering, stronger demand from the U.S., at least, should support Singapore's economy over the coming quarters. We still expect Singapore's trade-dependent economy to grow by around 3.0% this year and 3.5% in 2015." The economy grew 1.2% on-quarter and 2.4% on-year in the third quarter, according to government statistics released early Tuesday. Capital Economics says it expects the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  to continue holding its monetary policy steady into April, as it did Tuesday. "Any attempts to push growth much higher would probably cause inflation to rise," it writes. (jake.watts@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @jmwatts_) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0412 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Australian dollar's roughly 6% slide since early September is good news for Cochlear (COH.AU), according to its chief executive, who says the world's biggest bionic ear manufacturer books around 95% of its sales offshore. The Aussie is trading at around $0.88, down from around $0.94 in August, amid expectations the U.S. will tighten monetary policy and that China's economy is cooling. "We win if the Australian dollar goes down and we lose if it appreciates," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chris Roberts\f28 \uc2 \f2  tells The Wall Street Journal, adding, however, that high volatility makes the impact on Cochlear a little less clear. "There's certainly a school of thought that says the Australian dollar is over-valued, but I've stopped trying to predict where it'll go," Roberts says. (Ross.Kelly@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0406 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Jefferies says attrition remains "a worry" at India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys (500209.BY)\f28 \uc2 \f2 , as the company is losing 10,000 employees a quarter. The company's recent bonus payouts and promotions--and more importantly seasonality--may reduce attrition in the December quarter, Jefferies says. Despite that, it's too early to call it a declining trend, it says; adding that it would require three or four quarters of sustained improvement to create a trend. On Friday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it paid out 100% of the variable component of salaries to employees. Though the compensation hasn't created an impact on the company's second quarter operating margins, Jefferies warns that it could be a disruptive long-term trend. The stock is down 0.4% at INR3,929.30. The Sensex is up 0.4%.(dhanya.thoppil@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0402 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Risk assets are very bid this morning in Asia after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its 14-day repo rate at the Open-Market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from 3.5% to 3.4%, raising hopes of broader-based easing, such as a cut in the required reserve ratio or benchmark rate, says Sue Trinh, strategist with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Royal Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2 . She adds, however, that she believes those expectations won't be met, similar to the previous two times that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chinese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reduced the 14-day repo rate. The latest cut follows a series of modest, targeted easing measures that Beijing has deployed in the past few months to help small business and public housing, she says. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  previously cut the 14-day rate from 3.8% to 3.7% on July 29 and from 3.7% to 3.5% on Sept. 18. (wynne.wang@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KBC \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0353 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Taiwan food stocks fall 1.6% versus the Taiex's 0.6% gain as investors, consumers and government grow more alarmed by recent food safety scandals. At the center of the food scare is the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ting Hsin International Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which caused an uproar by making cooking oil out of oil meant for animal feed. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wei Chuan Foods\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1201.TW), a unit of Ting Hsin that used the bad oil in some of its products, falls by 7% (the maximum allowable daily limit) for the second straight session to NT$27.25. Cathay Securities analyst Chien Boryi says there is no sign for a near-term rebound in Wei Chuan shares. Tingyi's Taiwan depositary receipts (910322.TW) drops 2.1% to NT$37.20; Tingyi is Ting Hsin's subsidiary and owns the noodle brand Master Kong. Taiwan's President Ma Ying-jeou on Monday called on the public to boycott the enterprises embroiled in the food scandals. Local governments have banned public schools from using products sold by the firms, and Ma has asked his cabinet to set up a task force to look at the issue. Taiwan's financial regulator has said it will back up a bank if it chooses to freeze loans to Ting Hsin.(fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 October 14, 2014 02:29 ET (06:29 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141014eaae000am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
