\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Supported as Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Slump -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,917 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Januar 2014\par 02:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.0500-6.0538   6.0406-6.0600 \par USD/TWD    30.160-30.430   30.000-30.500 \par USD/KRW     1,074-1,080     1,070-1,083 \par USD/SGD    1.2760-1.2800   1.2708-1.2813 \par USD/MYR    3.3200-3.3325   3.3120-3.3400 \par USD/THB     32.80-32.89     32.50-33.00 \par USD/PHP     45.20-45.38     45.00-45.50 \par USD/IDR    12,020-12,210   12,000-12,278 \par USD/INR     61.87-62.00     61.80-62.37 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation lower. A steep drop in the U.S. dollar index triggered by U.S. bond yields falling is likely to imply a lower USD/CNY benchmark rate set by the PBOC Friday. Spot USD/CNY, which closed at 6.0517 on Thursday, may hence fall under the psychological barrier at 6.0500. Investors may be slightly shaken by the poor HSBC China flash manufacturing PMI for January released yesterday that showed a contraction in manufacturing activity versus expectations for a smaller drop. The ongoing turmoil in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly in Argentina and Turkey which suffered steep falls overnight, is unlikely to affect the yuan very much. Traders are expecting activity in the yuan to subside as the Lunar New Year holidays approach next week. The PBOC has been injecting liquidity into the money market this week to cap spikes in short-term lending rates - sparked by demand for loans ahead of the holidays. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.0500 (psychological support), then at 6.0406 (record low), before 6.0366 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0538 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.0600 (psychological resistance), before 6.0700 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--upside bias. The steep overnight drop in the U.S. dollar index could take the legs off the USD/TWD rally for now, but the technical upside bias will persist in the near term if the dollar ends Friday above 30.160 and therefore still within the Bollinger uptrend channel. The greenback fell Thursday as stock investors appeared to liquidate their positions in favor of safe haven U.S. bonds, sending the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield lower which weighed on the U.S. dollar. Traders will still be wary of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the Taiwan dollar weak, and may hence look to buy USD/TWD on dips. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help its exporters maintain a price advantage via a cheaper \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relative to trade rivals. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.160 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.900 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.430 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--upside bias. USD/KRW spikes higher Friday as Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors get spooked by the collapse in other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the world, particularly in Argentina where the peso was devalued. The South Korea won dropped to as low as 1,077.8 to the dollar, representing a 0.4% fall versus Thursday's closing. Stock markets in Asia are down on cue from the 1.1% overnight drop in the Dow Jones Industrial Average. The won may weaken further toward 1,080 due to the general risk aversion that has emerged overnight. The South Korea won could however find some support from the IMF comments on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slightly undervalued and that \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  should be more transparent in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,074 (base of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,070 (psychological support), before 1,067 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 1,080 (psychological resistance), then at 1,083 (top of weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. The technical upside bias for USD/SGD remains in effect as along as the greenback stays above 1.2761 and thereby within the Bollinger uptrend channel. Traders have ignored the overnight drop in the U.S. dollar index and are instead focused on risk aversion in emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sparked by the abrupt devaluation of the Argentine peso overnight. The overnight fall in U.S. stocks accompanied by investors buying bonds also suggests a liquidation of risk assets is underway that could hurt Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  further. USD/SGD could soon hit the 5-month peak of 1.2859 last seen in August. Upside for the USD/SGD may be mitigated by investor sentiment that the Singapore dollar is less vulnerable than other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and therefore will not weaken as much. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2760 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2708 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2700 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2813 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2859 (5-month peak).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is likely to be well-supported and could rally toward the 3.3500 psychological barrier next, though traders suspect the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  near the 3.3350-3.3360 level to stem ringgit weakness. USD/MYR technical upside momentum appears strong on the daily chart, with no sign of exhaustion to the USD/MYR rally yet. The collapse of the Argentine peso overnight, which fell as much as 14% due to a sudden devaluation by the government, is sparking fear amongst those invested in Asian emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the ringgit. A full-blown risk aversion scenario is brewing as stocks slide on cue from overnight U.S. markets and U.S bonds rallied - indicative of a flight to safe haven assets. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3200 (psychological support), then at 3.3120 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3325 (Wednesday's 5-month peak), then at 3.3350 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level), before 3.3400 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--likely upside bias. The technical upside bias for USD/THB will be reinstated if the dollar climbs back into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now awaits at 32.89. The overnight collapse of the Argentine peso is spooking Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders who fear a contagion effect might reach Asia as investors reduce their risk appetite for emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general. The repeated escalations in violence in the Bangkok political protests will continue to weigh on the baht, though its effect may be less apparent as most speculative bearish bets have already been priced in. Speculative investors are largely already positioned for baht weakness, creating a situation where fresh sellers are lacking, thus leaving less potential for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall further. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.80 (psychological support), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 32.89 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 33.00 (psychological resistance), before 33.13 (4-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. The dollar is likely to rally again as investors seek the safety of the U.S. dollar after the selloff in stocks overnight and the mauling of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Argentina and Turkey. \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem peso weakness is likely if USD/PHP rises to the 3.5-year high of 45.38 notched on Wednesday. Technical analysis of the daily chart suggests USD/PHP is likely to stay buoyant as long as the daily Bollinger uptrend channel which now supports at 44.77 remains in effect. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.20 (psychological support), then at 45.00 (psychological support), before 44.77 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.38 (Wednesday's 3.5-year peak), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation higher. Rupiah weakness could accelerate if USD/IDR enters the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that begins at 12,210. An emerging market assets selloff on the other side of the world threatens to upset investor sentiment in Asia. The sudden devaluation of the Argentine peso, which follows record lows set by the Turkish lira, is causing ripples in Asia. Investors may seek to reduce their holdings of high-yielding risky \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the rupiah as a global risk aversion brews. Ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said last week that Indonesia's external debt is still a concern and that political risks could rise ahead of elections later this year. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,020 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 12,000 (psychological support), before 11,800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,210 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,278 (5-year high), before 12,300 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 23 Jan 2014 20:01 EDT  USD/Asia Supported as Emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  Slump -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation higher. USD/INR may get a boost higher due to a shift in investor sentiment away from emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and toward safe haven assets such as the U.S. dollar - sparked by the abrupt devaluation of the Argentine peso overnight. USD/INR may rally past the strong resistance near 62.00 where the psychological trading barrier combines with the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. There could be room on the upside if the USD/INR closes above 62.00 Friday. The next obvious target will be the top of the daily Ichimoku Cloud at 62.37. The overnight fall in the U.S. stock market coupled with the rally in U.S. Treasurys suggests a major risk aversion could be taking place. Investors typically sell stocks and buy bonds when they are looking to reduce risk. The reduction in risk appetite will affect Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly high-yielding ones such as the rupiah and the rupee. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.87 (base of daily Ichimoku Cloud), then at 61.80 (psychological support), before 61.59 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.00 (psychological resistance and 20-day Bollinger mid), then at 62.37 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone),before 62.42 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 23, 2014 20:01 ET (01:01 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140124ea1o0006x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
