\par\par \b \uc2 USD/Asia Well Bid as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Yield Rises -- Asia Daily  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,937 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2014\par 02:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The following are projected trading ranges and outlooks for nine secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs in Asia today: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par           Immediate Range  Larger Range \par USD/CNY    6.0500-6.0546   6.0406-6.0600 \par USD/TWD    30.140-30.400   30.000-30.500 \par USD/KRW     1,065-1,070     1,063-1,073 \par USD/SGD    1.2756-1.2800   1.2704-1.2859 \par USD/MYR    3.3200-3.3325   3.3000-3.3400 \par USD/THB     32.88-33.00     32.50-33.13 \par USD/PHP     45.00-45.21     44.80-45.38 \par USD/IDR    12,010-12,210   12,000-12,278 \par USD/INR     61.59-62.00     61.50-62.37 \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (Ranges are calculated using recent highs and lows, information on the placement of option strikes, and technical analysis--Bollinger Bands, Fibonacci levels, trendlines and moving averages.)\par \par \uc2 USD/CNY--consolidation higher. The PBOC may set the benchmark USD/CNY exchange rate upwards a little to reflect a rebound in the U.S. dollar index overnight. Spot USD/CNY, which closed at 6.0513 on Wednesday may, therefore, consolidate higher toward the top of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel at 6.0546. \uc2 HSBC\uc2 's China Flash Manufacturing PMI will be released at 0145 GMT and may guide the way for regional equities as well as the Australia dollar. Recent movements in the U.S. bond market indicate that the trend of the stronger U.S. dollar is likely to continue. The benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury bond yield is climbing back toward the 3.0% barrier as investors sell bonds fearing the U.S. Federal Reserve is still on track to a further reduction in bond buying. As the Lunar New Year approaches China onshore short-term funding rates have started to spike again but the authorities have been injecting liquidity to prevent investor panic. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/CNY is at 6.0500 (psychological support), then at 6.0406 (record low), before 6.0373 (base of daily Bollinger downtrend channel). Immediate resistance is at 6.0546 (top of daily Bollinger downtrend channel), then at 6.0600 (psychological resistance), before 6.0700 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/TWD--upside bias. Both daily and weekly charts concur USD/TWD is likely to keep heading higher. The top of the daily Bollinger uptrend channel at 30.400 is the first technical resistance and therefore target for the dollar. A supportive tone for the dollar persists backed up by the overnight rebound in the U.S. 10-year Treasury yield. Traders are still wary of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the Taiwan dollar weak and are, therefore, biased to buy USD/TWD on dips. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been actively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help its exporters maintain a price advantage via a cheaper \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  relative to trade rivals. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 30.140 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.000 (psychological support), before 29.880 (20-day Bollinger mid support). Immediate resistance is likely at 30.400 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 30.500 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/KRW--upside bias. USD/KRW holds on to its short-term bullish bias helped by broad U.S. dollar strength overnight. The USD/KRW daily Bollinger uptrend channel currently supports the U.S. unit at 1,065 and may lead the way toward the January high of 1,071. The U.S. dollar is holding on to recent strength owing to growing sentiment that the U.S. Federal Reserve might continue to reduce bond buying at its next policy meeting. The South Korea won may find some support from IMF comments on Wednesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slightly undervalued and that \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  should be more transparent in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. Data on Wednesday showed South Korea's economic growth slowed to 0.9% in 4Q13 despite robust exports. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 1,065 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1,063 (daily Ichimoku Cloud support), before 1,061 (20-day Bollinger mid). Immediate resistance is at 1,070 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel and psychological resistance), then at 1,071 (January high), before 1,073 (weekly Bollinger uptrend channel).\par \par \uc2 USD/SGD--upside bias. USD/SGD may spike as stop-loss orders above 1.2800 may soon be triggered releasing a wave of U.S. dollar buying as investors cover their short USD/SGD positions. The daily Bollinger uptrend channel has been guiding the U.S. unit higher since Jan. 15 and will continue to unless USD/SGD closes below 1.2755 and thus breaks down from the channel. The bullish-USD signal on the weekly chart suggests USD/SGD may be headed for the 5-month peak of 1.2859 last seen in August. Traders are still mostly bullish on the U.S. unit--though selectively against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The fear of further reduction in U.S. Federal Reserve bond buying will likely keep USD/SGD supported on dips. Dow Jones technical analysis shows immediate support is at 1.2756 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 1.2704 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 1.2700 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 1.2800 (psychological resistance), then at 1.2807 (top of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 1.2859 (5-month peak).\par \par \uc2 USD/MYR--upside bias. USD/MYR is likely to keep rising toward the trading barrier at 3.3500 as the market regards the lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a sign Bank Negara will tolerate a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  so long as it is on par with the Singapore dollar and the Indonesia rupiah. This may encourage bearish bets on the ringgit in the near term. Technical upside momentum appears strong on the daily chart with no sign of exhaustion to the USD/MYR rally yet. U.S. dollar strength is underpinned by rising \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields--investors have been selling U.S bonds on fear that the U.S. Federal Reserve may again reduce bond buying. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 3.3200 (psychological support), then at 3.3080 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), before 3.3000 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 3.3325 (Wednesday's 5-month peak), then at 3.3350 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance), before 3.3400 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/THB--upside bias. The technical upside bias for USD/THB has been reinstated as the dollar has risen back into the daily Bollinger uptrend channel that now supports at 32.88. The repeated escalations in violence in Bangkok political protests will continue to weigh down the baht though the effect may be less apparent as most speculative bearish bets have already been priced in. Speculative investors are largely already positioned for baht weakness--creating a situation where fresh sellers are lacking--thus leaving less potential for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall further. However, the overall strength of the U.S. dollar--owing to niggling fears that the U.S. Federal Reserve may again reduce bond-buying at its next meeting--may propel USD/THB higher from here. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 32.88 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 32.80 (psychological support), before 32.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 33.00 (psychological resistance), before 33.13 (4-year high).\par \par \uc2 USD/PHP--upside bias. Despite the dollar's retreat Wednesday--possibly owing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem peso weakenss--the dollar still has a bullish bias and may climb back up to yesterday's high of 45.38. The USD/PHP is likely to stay buoyant as long as the daily Bollinger uptrend channel which now supports at 44.73 remains in effect. Investors are still fearful of a further withdrawal of U.S. Federal Reserve bond buying that would lead the benchmark 10-year Treasury yield higher and the dollar along with it. The U.S. unit continues to look biased higher against the euro and that may be a lead indicator for USD/PHP traders for now. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 45.00 (psychological support), then at 44.80 (psychological support), before 44.73 (base of daily Bollinger uptrend channel). Immediate resistance is likely at 45.21 (top of monthly Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 45.38 (Wednesday's 3.5-year peak), before 45.50 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 USD/IDR--consolidation higher. USD/IDR may rally toward the top of its current consolidation zone of 12,000-12,210 as the U.S. dollar index remains elevated helped by rising \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields and bullish technical signals for the dollar against the euro. USD/IDR may itself take on a bullish technical bias if it rises above 12,210 and thereby enters the daily Bollinger uptrend channel. Ratings agency \uc2 Moody's\uc2  said last week that Indonesia's external debt is still a concern and that political risks may rise ahead of elections later this year. The threat of further reductions in U.S. Federal Reserve bond buying will also depress the rupiah--many analysts have said that the Indonesia rupiah is most vulnerable in the region from a continued withdrawal of cheap U.S. dollar liquidity that has been funding foreign investment inflows into Indonesia since quantitative easing began in 2008. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support for spot USD/IDR is at 12,010 (20-day Bollinger mid support), then at 12,000 (psychological support), before 11,800 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is at 12,210 (daily Bollinger uptrend channel), then at 12,278 (5-year high), before 12,300 (psychological resistance).\par \par \uc2 22 Jan 2014 20:10 EDT  USD/Asia Well Bid as \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Yield Rises -- -2-\par \par \uc2 USD/INR--consolidation. The daily chart shows USD/INR has met strong resistance near 62.00 where the trading barrier combines with the daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance level as well as the 20-day Bollinger mid resistance. The rupee may therefore hold off the U.S dollar's broad advance. The U.S. unit is looking more resilient against the main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the benchmark U.S. 10-year Treasury yield climbs back toward the 3.0% barrier owing to bond investors selling U.S. Treasuries on fear the U.S. Federal Reserve may again reduce its bond buying. Macro investors are watching for signs the May 2014 elections may pave the way for greater economic reform and thereby foreign investment. Dow Jones technical analysis suggests immediate support is at 61.80 (psychological support), then at 61.59 (daily Bollinger downtrend channel), before 61.50 (psychological support). Immediate resistance is likely at 62.00 (psychological resistance and daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone), then at 62.03 (20-day Bollinger mid), before 62.37 (top of daily Ichimoku Cloud resistance zone).\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (This article is general financial information, not personalized investment advice, as it does not consider the unique circumstances affecting an individual reader's decision to buy or sell a specific security. Dow Jones does not warrant the accuracy, completeness or timeliness of the information in this article, and any errors will not be made the basis for any claim against Dow Jones. The author does not invest in the instruments or markets cited in this article.)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 22, 2014 20:10 ET (01:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140123ea1n0004c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
