\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX-Key political risks to watch in the Philippines\b0\par\par\uc2 By Manuel Mogato   \par \uc2 1,137 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2013\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MANILA, Feb 20 (Reuters) - The government and the country's largest Muslim rebel group have agreed a preliminary deal that may end a 40-year conflict that has killed more than 120,000 and displaced 2 million.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Benigno Aquino\uc2  hopes this will pave the way for economic growth and development in the south, a poor region but one that sits on considerable resources.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgraded its ratings of the county in October, following \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  in July, though S&P said further upgrades depend on Manila raising income levels or sustaining revenue reforms.\par \par \uc2 In 2012, the economy grew 6.6 percent, beating expectations and putting its rate of expansion second only to China.\par \par \uc2 Still, much of the country is dilapidated and vulnerable to natural disaster. Typhoon Bopha killed thousands in the south late last year, and heavy rains in August swamped huge swathes of Manila, killing more than 100 people and leaving hundreds of thousands homeless.\par \par \uc2 Internationally, by far the greatest concern is the South China Sea, contested waters where the U.S.-backed Philippines are increasingly running up against China.\par \par \uc2 RATINGS: (Unchanged unless stated:)\par \par \uc2 S&P: BB+\par \par \uc2 MOODY'S: Ba1 (Upgraded from Ba2 on Oct. 29)\par \par \uc2 FITCH: BB+\par \par \uc2 Following is a summary of political risks to watch:\par \par \uc2 INTERNAL SECURITY\par \par \uc2 Negotiators from the government and the Muslim rebel group Moro Islamic Liberation Front (MILF) reached a deal on a roadmap to set up a new autonomous Bangsamoro region in the south of the mainly Roman Catholic state, signalling an end to a long insurgency.\par \par \uc2 Still, the 11,000-member MILF is not the only active rebel group. Maoist guerrillas have attacked private mining projects on southern island Mindanao, destroying around $70 million worth of equipment, and threatening more attacks.\par \par \uc2 In general, internal security remains weak, persistently highlighted by foreign embassies in travel advisories, with law enforcement hobbled by corruption, lack of police resources, and easy availability of guns on the street.\par \par \uc2 What to watch:\par \par \uc2 - Implementation of the political deal to set up an autonomous region. This will include the demobilisation, disarmament and reintegration of former Muslim rebel fighters, imposition of local taxes to cut government subsidies, and revenue-sharing arrangements with oil and gas producers.\par \par \uc2 - Any more attacks on mines or other businesses, and how investors respond. The Philippine army has said it lacks the resources, so has asked firms to hire private militias to guard their businesses.\par \par \uc2 SOUTH CHINA SEA\par \par \uc2 The Philippines is at the centre of Asia's most likely military flashpoint: the South China Sea. Last year a regional summit failed to agree a position on the competing claims of various nations, and what appears to be the increasing alignment of Washington with Manila risks infuriating China.\par \par \uc2 In January the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  asked an international tribunal to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its longstanding dispute with China and declare that Beijing's claims are invalid, a move China rejected.\par \par \uc2 That came soon after U.S. and Philippine officials agreed on an increase in the number of U.S. military ships, aircraft and troops rotating through the Philippines, though officials from both countries say there is no plan to revive permanent U.S. military bases there.\par \par \uc2 Manila will not surrender claims to its exclusive economic zone, as defined by \uc2 the United Nations\uc2 , but it cannot hope to confront China militarily.\par \par \uc2 Beijing wants one-one-negotiations, but Manila and other claimants prefer a multilateral approach, which opens the way for an indirect role for the United States. China wants the United States to stay out of the dispute.\par \par \uc2 What to watch:\par \par \uc2 - New security arrangements between Washington and Manila to increase the U.S. military footprint in the Philippines, the U.S. fighter jets and warships the Philippines is able to buy, and how China responds to any Filipino military buildup.\par \par \uc2 - Any action taken by the tribunal of \uc2 the United Nations\uc2  Convention on the Law of the Sea (UNCLOS) on Manila's request for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - Fresh approaches by Manila to pursue its claims on the disputed Spratly Islands. Aquino has said Manila is looking into at least five other options to pursue its claims after China rejected arbitration, including asking for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the International Tribunal on the Law of the Sea (ITLOS) in Germany. Commercial activity in the South China Sea. Manila has accepted exploration bids on two oil and gas in the disputed areas, and an Anglo-Filipino company may start drilling oil wells later this year in the Reed Bank, another area claimed by China.\par \par \uc2 - Spending on upgrades of air and naval equipment, including radar stations. The Philippines plans to roll out $1.8 billion in defence spending in the next four years, but says its actions are not aggressive.\par \par \uc2 ECONOMIC GROWTH; CHURCH V STATE?\par \par \uc2 Mining firms want the Philippines to lift an 18-month moratorium on new projects, but this will not happen until lawmakers approve new legislation on mineral revenues and a presidential executive order is signed.\par \par \uc2 Congressional approval is likely to hold up permits further, stalling up to $12 billion in new investments planned over the next five years, including Southeast Asia's biggest undeveloped copper-gold mine, the $5.9 billion Tampakan project by global miner \uc2 Xstrata Plc\uc2  and Australia's \uc2 Indophil Resources NL\par \par \uc2 in the south of the country.\par \par \uc2 Still, the economy is performing well. With 6.6 percent growth in 2012, the Philippines is an example of expansion in contrast to Europe and the United States.\par \par \uc2 Authorities are struggling to control an inflow of capital that has pushed up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and threatens asset price bubbles, and government is concerned about the impact of a strong peso on the competitiveness of its exports and the growing outsourcing sector.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Parliament approved in December a highly controversial reproductive health bill, requiring the government to hand out contraceptives to poor people, a policy bitterly opposed by the Catholic church.\par \par \uc2 The move, the first time in more than a decade an elected politician has taken on the bishops and won, was a sign of Aquino's confidence and his bedrock of national support, but is unlikely to be the last battle between church and state.\par \par \uc2 What to watch:\par \par \uc2 - Possible ratings upgrades after the passage of new alcohol and tobacco sales tax rates. The tax reform measures are likely to push the Philippines towards investment grade.\par \par \uc2 - When the mining moratorium is lifted, and how quickly resources firms start work on new projects.\par \par \uc2 - Growth figures, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy moves.\par \par \uc2 - Political fallout from Aquino's challenge to the influential Roman Catholic bishops in pushing reform of contraception laws.\par \par \uc2 (Editing by Daniel Magnowski)\par \par \uc2 PHILIPPINES-RISKS/ (FACTBOX) | AUF | ABN | D | E | RBN | G | M | PHD | RNA | SI | UKI | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130220e92k0003m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
