\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Philippine peso up after \uc2 Moody's\uc2 ; exporters lift won, Taiwan dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2012\par 02:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgrades \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Ba1\par \par \uc2 * S.Korea \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  caution caps won's upside\par \par \uc2 * Taiwan dlr up on exporters; importers limit gains\par \par \uc2 (Adds text, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso turned higher on Monday after \uc2 Moody's\uc2  upgraded the country's sovereign ratings, while the South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar gained on month-end demand from exporters amid subdued trading.\par \par \uc2 The peso initially weakened to 41.275 per dollar during morning trade, but it reversed direction in the afternoon session after the rating agency's move.\par \par \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  upgraded the Philippines' foreign and local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  long-term bond ratings by one notch to Ba1 from Ba2, citing the country's improved economic performance and continued fiscal revenue buoyancy.\par \par \uc2 "At the moment, the market is looking for a catalyst to push the peso. Dollar/peso would be vulnerable to further downside with lack of corporate demand," said a European bank dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2 The dealer expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the peso's strength, but added: "one thing is clear that any upside (in dollar/peso) will be heavy."\par \par \uc2 The peso has gained 6.5 percent against the dollar so far this year, becoming the best performing emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Thomson Reuters data showed.\par \par \uc2 That came even as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted slowing down its appreciation along with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other central banks, which has curbed the peso's upside.\par \par \uc2 "Emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have lost much of their appreciation momentum on sustained worries about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . They also technically appeared to have risen too much, so more investors may want to take profits," said Yuna Park, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond analyst at \uc2 Dongbu Securities\uc2  in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 Investors were not confident enough about the global economic recovery despite signs of stable U.S. growth and due to uncertainty over the euro zone's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 Traders await Spain's request for a bailout, which would initiate the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's bond-buying programme and could push the euro out of its recent range.\par \par \uc2 Investors also kept a wary eye on Greece, after the country's opposition leader said his party would vote against an austerity package expected to go before parliament this week.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 The won hit 1,094.6 per dollar, its strongest since Oct. 28 last year on demand from exporters for month-end settlements.\par \par \uc2 But traders took profit on caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities to slow down the won's strength. Trading was also thin.\par \par \uc2 President Lee Myung-bak said in a speech that South Korea's comparative economic strength has been pushing the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher. This appreciation "makes difficulties for exporters," he said.\par \par \uc2 "The won may see short-term resistance around mid-1,090 once exporters' month-end deals are cleared this week," said a senior foreign bank dealer in Seoul.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar rose slightly on exporters' demand for settlements, while importers' bids for greenbacks limited the local unit's upside.\par \par \uc2 Interbank speculators hesitated to build up aggressive bets either way as overseas markets, especially in New York, are unlikely to provide market-moving factors due to Hurricane Sandy.\par \par \uc2 The storm is expected to slam into the U.S. East Coast on Monday night. Market participants in the New York area see a light trading day on Monday -- and possibly through Tuesday -- with some U.S. markets closed, as some offices in lower Manhattan's Financial District are in an evacuation zone.\par \par \uc2 RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The ringgit eased as traders covered dollar-short positions on a weaker euro, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 The Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  came under more pressure from some dollar demand from importers, they added.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Change on the day at 0645 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        79.67          79.66       -0.01\par  Sing dlr        1.2207         1.2208       +0.01\par  Taiwan dlr      29.255         29.300       +0.15\par  Korean won     1095.55        1097.00       +0.13\par  Baht             30.70          30.74       +0.13\par  Peso             41.17          41.21       +0.10\par  Rupiah         9610.00        9600.00       -0.10\par  Rupee            53.84          53.56       -0.51\par  Ringgit         3.0540         3.0385       -0.51\par  Yuan            6.2396         6.2489       +0.15\par  Change so far in 2012\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End pre