\par\par \b \uc2 DJ UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Fires Warning Shot On Strengthening Peso\b0\par\par\uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2012\par 14:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 --Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  as peso hits 4-year high\par \par \uc2 --Bank warns speculators it may curb NDFs\par \par \uc2 --Official moves may have only limited impact as investors flock to peso\par \par \uc2 (Combines previous stories, recasts throughout.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Martin Vaughan and Cris Larano \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  signaled Wednesday it's leery of the peso's recent surge and may increase its efforts to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas sold pesos for dollars in the market, traders said, and the bank announced it will review rules on nondeliverable forward contracts, a tool traders use to speculate on the direction of emerging-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Manila's authorities stepped in as the peso hit a four-year high, with the dollar falling to PHP41.60. The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rebounded after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announcement to PHP41.83 late in Asia trade. The bank's moves came before \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services upgraded the government's debt by a notch to just below investment grade.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Amando Tetangco soft-pedaled the moves, saying the peso's recent action is in line with a broader pick-up in appetite for risky \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It's appreciating just like most (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) in the region are, although admittedly it has moved more than the others in recent days," Mr. Tetangco told Dow Jones Newswires in a text message. "We are monitoring price action and market behavior to determine (any) unusual activity."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The peso is up 5% against the dollar this year and his risen 4.5% since May 24 alone. That's in sharp contrast to most of its Asian peers, weighed by global risk aversion as the euro-zone debt crisis has roiled markets in recent months: Indonesian rupiah is down 3.0% this year, while the Malaysian ringgit and Thai baht are roughly flat.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors have been drawn to the peso for a number of reasons. The Philippine economy grew at a standout pace of 6.4% in the first quarter, and reforms by President Benigno Aquino III have narrowed the fiscal deficit. The peso's gains have been driven by foreign buying of Philippine shares, which increased 59% in the first half of the year.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thomas Harr, Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Standard Chartered, said the Philippines "is having a little bit of a moment similar to what Indonesia had between mid-2009 and mid-2011," when that country's assets, such as bonds and the rupiah, posted big gains on expectations of sovereign credit upgrades.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may struggle to curb the peso via NDF restrictions since it can only directly control what domestic banks do in this offshore market. "Any rule changes will be modest and limited and will have only a short-term impact on the peso," Mr. Harr said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Tetangco said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will review regulations on NDFs and "special deposit accounts"--fixed-term deposits by banks, trust entities and other financial institutions, used primarily to manage liquidity due to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  inflows--"because these two can be possible entry points for speculation."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those statements are a "warning shot" to let markets know the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is watching, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Santitarn Sathirathai.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But while the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was in the market Wednesday, it typically doesn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as aggressively as its counterparts in such places as Indonesia, South Korea and Taiwan.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And the Philippine authorities aren't greatly concerned about supporting the country's exports, Mr. Santitarn said, because inflation remains low, keeping the peso competitive in inflation-adjusted terms.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rather, he said, what worries the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is the exchange rate's impact on remittance flows from overseas workers. A growing segment of the population depends on those flows to purchase daily necessities, and a weakening dollar means the paychecks from overseas will translate into fewer pesos.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Manila-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may consider cutting interest rates to lessen the peso's attractiveness, especially if June inflation, out Thursday stays below the bank's 3%-5% target range.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Martin Vaughan at martin.vaughan@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 04, 2012 08:08 ET (12:08 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120704e874002u4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
