\par\par \b \uc2 Philippines - Market factors to watch - Dec 6\b0\par\par\uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2011\par 01:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MANILA, Dec 5 (Reuters) - Here are news stories and press reports which may influence local financial markets on Tuesday:\par \par \uc2 WHAT IS HAPPENING TODAY IN THE PHILIPPINES:\par \par \uc2 - National Statistics Office to release inflation data for November, 9:00 a.m. [0100 GMT]\par \par \uc2 - National Statistics Office to release October Producer Price Survey\par \par \uc2 - Bureau of Treasury holds 25-year Treasury bond auction, 1:00 p.m. [0500 GMT]\par \par \uc2 - Energy Secretary Jose Rene Almendras is guest speaker at Energy Investment Forum, Eastwood Richmonde Hotel, 9:00 a.m. [0100 GMT]\par \par \uc2 - World Bank's Water and Sanitation Programme to launch its Economic Assessment of Sanitation \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  study, Sapphire Room, Crowne Plaza Hotel, Quezon City, 8:30 a.m. [0030 GMT]\par \par \uc2 REUTERS NEWS - PHILIPPINES > Philippine c.bank: Ready to ease if growth slows > Philippines' SM Prime eyes 300-ha Cebu property > FACTBOX-Philippines' emerging coal industry > Foreigners buy Philippines shares in latest week > Key political risks to watch in the Philippines\par \par \uc2 > Philippine Marcventures to sell ore to nickel firm\par \par \uc2 LOCAL PRESS REPORTS\par \par \uc2 (Reuters has not verified these stories)\par \par \uc2 - Electronics exports could plunge by as much as 25 percent this year, lower than a previous forecast, as manufacturers expect results to hit new lows, but shipments may rebound to grow 10 percent next year, the head of industry group SEIPI said. (BUSINESSWORLD)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Philippine Long Distance Telephone Co\uc2  will conduct a mandatory tender offer for the remaining 48.5 percent of its newly acquired unit \uc2 Digital Telecommunications Philippines Inc\uc2 .. (ALL PAPERS)\par \par \uc2 - The feasibility study for an express railway line connecting Manila to the Clark Special Economic Zone in the north will start early next year, with bidding for the project to take place soon after the study is finished, a public works official said. (PHILIPPINE DAILY INQUIRER, MANILA BULLETIN, MALAYA)\par \par \uc2 - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has given seven banks the green light to establish 162 new branches in restricted areas that include eight cities in the capital, as part of the regulator's bank branching liberalisation efforts. (ALL PAPERS)\par \par \uc2 - \uc2 Apex Mining Co. Inc\uc2  said on Monday its copper-gold exploration programme near its operating Maco gold mine in the southern Compostela Valley province has shown significant potential. (MANILA STANDARD TODAY, BUSINESSMIRROR)\par \par \uc2 - The Bases Conversion and Development Authority sees higher revenue from the Bonifacio South property following the decision of SM Land Inc of the SM Group to improve its unsolicited proposal for the development of the 33.1 hectare property. (PHILIPPINE DAILY INQUIRER,MALAYA)\par \par \uc2 MARKET NEWS > Global stocks, euro lose steam on downgrade woes > Yields sink close to zero at German, Dutch sales > Oil erases most gains on Europe ratings worry > Gold falls on technical selling, euro debt fears \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par > Asian stocks firmer before EU summit              \tab \par      \tab \par -------------- MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0041 ---------------------\tab \par                 INSTRUMENT    LAST      PCT CHG    NET CHG \par S&P 500                         1257.08      1.03      12.80\par USD/JPY                           77.76      0.00       0.00\par US 10YR                            2.06      1.29       0.03\par SPOT GOLD                       1723.55      0.12       2.06\par US CRUDE                         100.58 