\par\par \b \uc2 Philippines Finance Minister:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Allows Mkt To Determine Exchange Rate\b0\par\par\uc2 166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2011\par 19:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON (Dow Jones)--Philippines Finance Secretary Cesar Purisima said Thursday that it is in the country's greater interest to focus on economic fundamentals and leave the level of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to markets.\par \par \uc2 His comments come as emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Philippine peso, are seeing big drops on rising risk aversion.\par \par \uc2 Purisima said at a Washington speech that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows markets to determine the value of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  mainly to smooth out any disruptive movements.\par \par \uc2 "Outside of that the best thing we can do is invest in fundamentals," he said.\par \par \uc2 His comments would suggest that \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy makers aren't inclined toward any dramatic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but would rather make smaller moves when needed to smooth out volatile swings.\par \par \uc2 "The best thing is really to leave it up to the markets," he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Anjali Cordeiro; Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2200 [ 09-22-11 1440ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020110922e79m000kl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
