\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Philippines Comfortable With Peso Level; Monitoring For Disruptive Moves\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2011\par 10:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- The Philippines is comfortable with current level of its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , finance secretary Purisima says\par \par \uc2 -- The Philippines is closely monitoring movements of peso against Asian peers\par \par \uc2 -- The Philippines aims to step up spending on infrastructure, social sector\par \par \uc2 (Rewrites first paragraph, adds finance secretary's comments on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the second and fourth paragraphs and budget deficit in the fifth and sixth paragraphs, background on suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the third paragraph)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Gaurav Raghuvanshi \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Philippines is comfortable with the current level of its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and is monitoring for any disruptive movements of the peso, the nation's finance chief said Thursday, less than a month after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reportedly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the U.S. dollar from a three-year low.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Right now we believe that we are within the comfortable band of exchange rate that moves within (the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of) our peer countries. We cannot stop appreciation (of the Philippine peso). Most of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the world are appreciating against the U.S, dollar and that's something that we need to adjust to," Cesar Purisima, the finance secretary, told reporters in Singapore. "What we are trying to monitor closely is disruptive movements."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On July 26, the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was estimated to have bought as much as US$200 million at various levels as the peso climbed to its highest in three years. The U.S. dollar hit a low of PHP41.90 on Aug. 1 but has since recovered a bit, trading at PHP42.50 at 0750 GMT Thursday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Purisima, who is also a member of the monetary board of the Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , said the nation's authorities are monitoring the movements of the peso's peers in the Asian region and that "we let the market determine the peso-dollar exchange rate."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He also highlighted how the government racked up a budget deficit of only PHP17 billon in the first half of this year, much smaller than the target of about PHP150 billion for the period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "That shows that we are way ahead of our (budget deficit) program. We're doing so much better. In fact, our challenge is how to spend more," he said, adding that the government is trying to build capacity in its institutions to step up spending on infrastructure and social sector.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier, addressing delegates at an investor conference organized by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Credit Suisse\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Purisima said financial markets are likely to remain turbulent until global issues, such as the U.S. debt burden and the sovereign debt crisis in Europe, are addressed.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If you see what happened on Wall Street last night, the market turbulence of the last week appears far away. But we will get more turbulence unless the problems are addressed," he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Purisima also said that the Association of Southeast Asian Nations should work on relying less on exports to the U.S. and Europe and focus more on increasing domestic consumption.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Gaurav Raghuvanshi, Dow Jones Newswires; +65 64154 152; venkat.pr@dowjones.com [ 18-08-11 0827GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110818e78i000m3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
47
