\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah at 4-yr high on c.bank; \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  caps gains\b0\par\par\uc2 1,019 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 03:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Indonesia c.bank sees more room for rupiah's rise\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Indonesia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Singapore, Thailand spotted\par \par \uc2 * Won, Taiwan dlr at 2-wk high (Updates with text, prices)\par \par \uc2 By Jongwoo Cheon\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 4 (Reuters) - The rupiah hit a near four-year high against the dollar after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  signalled on Friday it was willing to use the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains in its battle with inflation even though it was seen buying dollars in an effort to control the rupiah's rise.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its benchmark rate on hold at its policy meeting, but said that it would gradually lift borrowing costs in the future and that it saw room for the rupiah to strengthen further without hurting export competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 "The bank confirmed today that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength is helping the inflation problem," said Christopher Gothard, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in Hong Kong.\par \par \uc2 "BI is still attempting to manage the rupiah's gains, with \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  designed more to slow the gain and make it more orderly, rather than stop it altogether," Gothard said.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in other Asian countries, such as Singapore, Philippines and Thailand, were also spotted buying dollars. Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  seemed designed to slow their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' gains rather than to weaken them because that would exacerbate inflation pressures.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH\par \par \uc2 The Dollar slid by up to 0.3 percent against the rupiah to 8,780, the rupiah's strongest level since June 2007, from Thursday's close of 8,803.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors continued to sell the pair, which has room to fall to 8,755, the low in June, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was on guard, dealers said.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept its overnight interest rate at 6.75 percent as forecast by a slender majority of economists, saying it would adjust the rate in stages if necessary and closely monitor rising core inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Today's decision implies BI will be more comfortable doing the tightening via \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But slowly,, as they will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a strategist of a U.S. Bank in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Taiwan dollar slid to a two-week low as foreign investors sold the pair and on foreigners' continuous stock purchases.\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Taiwan dollar touched 29.310, the lowest since Feb 18.\par \par \uc2 WON\par \par \uc2 Dollar/won hit a near two-week low as continuous foreign purchases of Seoul stocks prompted stop-loss dollar sales.\par \par \uc2 The pair fell to as low as 1,114.1, the lowest since Feb. 21, but it found support from caution over dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and importers' demand around mid-1,110.\par \par \uc2 "They (the authorities) don't want it to go above 1,130, but they will buy dollars at 1,110 anyway even if the Bank of Korea raises interest rates," said a dealer in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors reported their biggest net buying of local stocks in two months.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 Dollar/peso edged down on fixing demand and profit-taking from the peso's recent gains, but the Philippines's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted buying dollars to check the peso's strength.\par \par \uc2 Bangko Sentral Pilipinas (BSP) was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 43.25-27, dealers said, even though it said higher February inflation supported its view that the scope for keeping rates steady has narrowed.\par \par \uc2 "All central banks in Asia, including the BSP, are facing the same dilemma -- how to check inflation and to support exports at the same time," says a senior European bank dealer in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Philippine February inflation hit its highest since May, raising the likelihood the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will lift rates this month for the first time since the global financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Dollar/peso may break through its support at 43.25, the low of on Feb 21 and the 61.8 percent of the November-January rise, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  take actions to curb inflation.\par \par \uc2 A break of this support will see a decline to 42.90, the 76.4 percent of the rise. Strong resistance for pair is seen at 43.60 and 43.90. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR                                  \tab \par   Change on the day at 0750 GMT\tab \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen        82.41          82.41       +0.00\par   Sing dlr        1.2670         1.2677       +0.06\par   Taiwan dlr      29.363         29.542       +0.61\par   Korean won     1114.50        1119.90       +0.48\par   Baht             30.47          30.47   