\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Indonesia, Manila prop up  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  as emerging markets tumble\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gde Anugrah Arka and Sonya Angraini   \par \uc2 665 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2010\par 04:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, May 7 (Reuters) - Central banks in Indonesia and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up their sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday as worries about Greece's debt crisis spurred investors to dump emerging market assets.\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding rupiah <IDR> has tumbled 3 percent against the dollar this week, among the worst hit in Asia, while the peso has skidded 2.7 percent as part of a broad sell-off in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a move into safer assets.\par \par \uc2 Though worries about Greece's problems spreading to the rest of Europe are likely to persist for some time, Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the country's solid fiscal and economic fundamentals would support for the rupiah in the long run.\par \par \uc2 "We don't see (the weakening rupiah) as too worrying because fundamentals are still good. This will just be temporary,"Darmin Nasution, Bank Indonesia's senior deputy governor, told reporters on Friday.\par \par \uc2 But he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been closely following the rupiah's moves since earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always in the market," he added.\par \par \uc2 In the Philippines, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Diwa Guinigundo offered similar reassurances to nervous investors, saying the country can withstand shocks in financial markets as domestic consumption remains healthy and its foreign reserves are at a comfortable level.\par \par \uc2 "In case there is a double dip, we are well placed to absorb the shocks. On balance, we have what it takes to weather another crisis," Guinigundo told reporters.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell just over 1 percent on Friday to 9,300 per dollar, a two-month low, but later pared some of the losses on suspected cental bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still up 2 percent against the dollar so far this year. It had gained nearly 6 percent through April before Greece's debt crisis escalated and profit taking set in.\par \par \uc2 Investor sentiment toward Indonesian assets was also undermined by Finance Minister Sri Mulyani Indrawati's decision on Wednesday to resign, as she played a key role in improving the economy.\par \par \uc2 Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  in Singapore, expects the rupiah to find support near 9,400/9,500.\par \par \uc2 "The rupiah has lost ground on unwinding of risk exposures, including liquidation of Indonesian bonds, on the global stock rout as well as the finance minister's resignation," she said.\par \par \uc2 "But the fundamentals for Indonesia remain positive and we expect the rupiah to be sought after again when the dust settles."\par \par \uc2 One of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governors, Budi Mulya, echoed Bank Indonesia's vigilance.\par \par \uc2 "Bank Indonesia (BI) will continue to ensure a stable rupiah that reflects its underlying fundamentals," Mulya said in a phone text message.\par \par \uc2 "At times of substantial capital inflow, BI safeguarded rupiah stability through its sterilisation, and that has built up \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to more than $78 billion. Similarly, in the event of capital outflows, BI is also committed to safeguard the rupiah's stability."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also reiterated its commitment to ensure a free capital market and dispel concerns of any capital controls.\par \par \uc2 In the Phillipines, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sold dollars to slow the peso's decline, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> was down 0.9 percent at 45.78 per dollar despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Among other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the South Korean won <KRW=> fell 4.1 percent on the week, its biggest weekly fall since February 2009.\par \par \uc2 Foreign investors had flocked to emerging Asian assets earlier this year as the region's economic growth far eclipsed that of the West, but a spike in volatility in recent weeks has prompted some to scale back their positions and book profits. (Reporting Gde Anugrah Arka, Sonya Angraini and Kevin Yao; Writing by Yoko Nishikawa; Editing by Sara Webb & Kim Coghill)\par \par \uc2 INDONESIA-ECONOMY/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|PHD|IF|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100507e6570005s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
