outnumber optimists with a consumer confidence index of -27.6 percent this quarter from the -36 registered in the fourth quarter of last year, but sentiment on personal finance and the economy has improved, data from a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll showed. (BUSINESSWORLD, PHILIPPINE DAILY INQUIRER, THE MANILA TIMES)\par \par \uc2  - \uc2 San Miguel Corp\uc2   said it hired international consultants that will study the possibility of building a bullet train railway running from the north to south of the Luzon island, and it planning to submit its proposals to government by the end of the year. (THE PHILIPPINE STAR)\par \par \uc2  - Agriculture Undersecretary Salvador Salacup said that there is ample supply of rice and other basic food items in the country until the third quarter of 2010 despite the dry spell caused by the El Nino phenomenon, with 8,500 metric tons of rice being stored across the Philippines as buffer stock. (BUSINESSWORLD)\par \par \uc2  - \uc2 Trans-Asia Oil and Energy Development Corp\uc2   said it plans to raise as much as 2.2 billion pesos through the sale of new shares within the year, proceeds from which will partly finance its wind power projects and its bid for state power assets. (PHILIPPINE DAILY INQUIRER, THE PHILIPPINE STAR)\par \par \uc2  - Metropolitan Bank & Trust  unit Global Business Power Corp said it wants to venture into renewable energy sources and has started to evaluate potential hydro and biomass projects in the Visayas, having already gained a foothold in the power sector with its coal-fired power projects in that region. (THE MANILA TIMES)\par \par \uc2  - The Philippine Stock Exchange approved the 22.3 billion peso initial public offering of \uc2 JG Summit Holdings\uc2   unit Cebu Air in its meeting on Wednesday, with \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  and \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  as its lead managers, stock exchange sources said. (MANILA STANDARD TODAY)\par \par \uc2  MARKET NEWS  > Wall St ends flat after aucti