\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won leads slide; c.banks support rupiah, peso\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Februar 2010\par 03:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Dollar/won NDFs jump, won vols pick up\par \par \uc2  * C.banks in Indonesia, \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Swiss c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  * Investors jittery ahead of U.S. jobs data, G7\par \par \uc2  By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Feb 5 (Reuters) - The South Korean won led Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower on Friday as investors dumped riskier assets on jitters over debt problems in Europe, prompting central banks in Indonesia and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Asian stocks dipped, while dollar extended its gains from the previous day due to investor anxiety about sovereign debt in Greece, Portugal and Spain sparked a sell-off in the euro.\par \par \uc2  But the euro leapt against the Swiss franc as the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its own \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The ero earlier plunged to a 15-month low against the franc <EURCHF=>. [ID:nTOE614043]\par \par \uc2  Weakness in the Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso prompted their central banks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.\par \par \uc2 "I would place them in the category of Asian central banks that are genuinely concerned about volatility of their illiquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  so would not be at all surprised if they stepped in to calm rupiah and peso on what is a very nervous count-down to payrolls," said \uc2 Westpac\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sean Callow.\par \par \uc2  Asian central banks usually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by buying dollars to limit the rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support local exporters, but also step in to smooth sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls.\par \par \uc2  WON\par \par \uc2  The spot won <KRW=> tumbled about 2 percent in early trade to 1,176.9 per dollar but later steadied near 1,170.\par \par \uc2  The won, which has lost more than 4 percent since Jan. 11, faces further weakness after a dip below the 100-day moving average at 1,162 on Friday.\par \par \uc2  Offshore dollar/won NDFs <KRWNDFOR=> jumped amid jitters over sovereign debt risks in Europe, but they later trimmed gains as Korean exporters start selling.\par \par \uc2  One-month NDFs steadied near 1,170 after hitting as high as 1,178.6 compared to Thursday's close at 1,174.\par \par \uc2  "We see strong selling by exporters, funds are staying aside now. It was a drama last night, with euro collapsing and everything squeezed. I think all want to take a breath before U.S. non-farm payrolls and G7 meeting this weekend," said a Singapore-based NDF trader.\par \par \uc2  Manwhile, won's implied volatilities <KRWVOL> hit 15 percent from 14 percent on Thursday as the spot dips.\par \par \uc2  "Won vols are well bid as dollar/won moves higher," said an option trader.\par \par \uc2  RUPIAH, PESO\par \par \uc2  The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> fell as far as 9,410 per dollar -- down 1 percent from Thursday's close -- as traders spotted official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the unit.\par \par \uc2  "BI (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is interferring in the market just to stabilise the rupiah -- they are selling dollars at 9,410," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> shed 0.8 percent to 46.53 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  "We suspect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling dollars at today's high," said a trader in Manila.\par \par \uc2  The rupiah has shed 3 percent since early January while the peso has lost 2 percent.  Change on the day at 0705 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.66          88.95       -0.79\par  Sing dlr        1.4201         1.4208       +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      32.065         32.020       -0.14\par  Korean won     1168.95        1150.90       -1.54\par  Baht             33.17          33.09       -0.24\par  Peso             46.47          46.17       -0.65\par  Rupiah         9390.00        9315.00       -0.80\par  Rupee            46.54          46.25       -0.62\par  Ringgit         3.4390         3.4210       -0.52\par  Yuan            6.8274         6.8269       -0.01\par  Change so far in 2010\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.66          92.90       +3.61\par  Sing dlr        1.4201         1.4053       -1.04\par  Taiwan dlr      32.065         32.030       -0.11\par  Korean won     1168.95        1164.50       -0.38\par  Baht             33.17          33.32       +0.45\par  Peso             46.47          46.20       -0.58\par  Rupiah         9390.00        9420.00       +0.32\par  Rupee            46.54          46.54       -0.01\par  Ringgit         3.4390         3.4220       -0.49\par  Yuan            6.8274         6.8270       -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Reporting by Kevin Yao; Editing by Kazunori Takada)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highl