\par\par \b \uc2 Philippines Deputy Governor: Monitoring Closely USD/PHP Moves\b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2009\par 07:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 KUALA LUMPUR (Dow Jones)--The Philippines' \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Diwa C Guinigundo said Monday that the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas is monitoring closely the movements of the peso against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 "It is something we do on a daily basis," he said on the sidelines at a conference in Kuala Lumpur.\par \par \uc2 The peso reached a 13-month high Thursday, with the dollar falling to PHP46.25.\par \par \uc2 Guinigundo said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't set a target exchange level for the peso but "the monitoring was to ensure that the movements were orderly."\par \par \uc2 He declined to say if the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market recently.\par \par \uc2 - By K.P, Lee, Dow Jones Newswires; (603) 2026 1233; kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com [ 19-10-09 0533GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020091019e5aj000b0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
