\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah jumps,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  suspected as peso rises\b0\par\par\uc2 722 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2009\par 08:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah, ringgit lead Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rally against dollar\par \par \uc2 * Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen trying to cap peso\par \par \uc2 * Baht falls amid concerns over Thai king's health\par \par \uc2 By Kevin Yao\par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah and Malaysian ringgit led Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher against the beleaguered dollar on Thursday, but the baht came under selling pressure amid concerns over the Thai king's health.\par \par \uc2 Central banks in Taiwan, South Korea and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rise in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a 14-month low against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  <.DXY> as comments by the head of Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  encouraged investors to buy the higher-yielding Australian dollar, which helped buoy emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Dollar weakness, positive commodities and emerging market sentiment from overnight promise further heaviness for the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs today," Emmanuel Ng, strategist at \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2 , said in a note.\par \par \uc2 RUPIAH, RINGGIT\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding rupiah <IDR=> jumped 0.8 percent to 9,290 per dollar, the highest since September 2008, as foreigners continued to buy stocks and bonds.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah, the top performer in Asia, has gained 18 percent against the dollar so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Some traders cautioned that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been tolerating the sharp gains to help check price rises, may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the rupiah rise further.\par \par \uc2 The ringgit <MYR=> rose as far as 3.347 per dollar, up 0.6 percent from Wednesday's close, the highest since August 2008.\par \par \uc2 "Obviously, the broad dollar weakness continues," said a trader.\par \par \uc2 PESO\par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> gained 0.4 percent to 46.25 per dollar, highest since Sept. 2008, as the dollar falters globally.\par \par \uc2 "BSP (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) abandoned its support at 46.45 and is now at 46.25," said a Manila-based trader, who added that offshore NDFs <PHPNDFOR=> pointed to more dollar depreciation.\par \par \uc2 A second trader believed the official dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday was not as aggressive as the previous day. "As always, I think they've been trying to support dollar/peso slowly," said the trader.\par \par \uc2 BAHT\par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> resumed its slide in line with heavy losses in Thai stocks on concerns over the health of Thailand's King Bhumibol Adulyadej. The baht hit a two-week low at 33.51 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "There has been more dollar buying. We think the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is largely taking a lead from the fast-sliding stock market in contrast with most rallying Asian bourses," a dealer said.\par \par \uc2 The health of the king is improving but he needs time-consuming physical therapy, a palace official said on Thursday after concerns over his health sparked a second day of foreign selling in Thailand's financial markets. [ID:nBKK412913]\par \par \uc2 ING was cautious about Thai markets.\par \par \uc2 "We view political risk as elevated, which leads us to recommend investors avoid all Thai financial assets," analysts at ING said in a note. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0555 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.37          89.42       +0.06\par  Sing dlr        1.3851         1.3900       +0.35\par  Taiwan dlr      32.206         32.242       +0.11\par  Korean won     1155.40        1164.80       +0.81\par  Baht             33.50          33.44       -0.18\par  Peso             46.26          46.45       +0.42\par  Rupiah         9305.00        9365.00       +0.64\par  Rupee            45.87          46.13       +0.58\par  Ringgit         3.3465         3.3680       +0.64\par  Yuan            6.8257         6.8265       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2009\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        89.37          90.60       +1.38\par  Sing dlr        1.3851         1.4340       +3.53\par  Taiwan dlr      32.206         32.860       +2.03\par  Korean won     1155.40        1259.50       +9.01\par  Baht             33.50          34.80       +3.88\par  Peso             46.26          47.52       +2.73\par  Rupiah         9305.00       11000.00      +18.22\par  Rupee            45.87          48.71       +6.20\par  Ringgit         3.3465         3.4500       +3.09\par  Yuan            6.8257         6.8230       -0.04\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Jan Dahinten)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020091018e5af0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
