\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 11\b0\par\par\uc2 1,844 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 September 2009\par 09:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =2ND UPDATE: JAPAN 2Q GDP CUT TO +0.6% DUE TO INVENTORY DROP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's gross domestic product grew less than initially reported in the April-June quarter, suggesting underlying weakness in nation's recovery as some key parts of the economy continue to struggle. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA AUG INDUS GROWTH PICKS UP, PRICE DROPS NARROW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Chinese economy continued to recover in August, as industrial expansion accelerated and investment growth remained robust, while price drops slowed, government data issued Friday showed. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP:CHINA AUG EXPORTS UP 3.4% VS JUL; IMPORTS UP 1% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's exports and imports both picked up for the third straight month on a month-on-month basis in August, although year-to-date trade continued to fall compared with the year-earlier period, government data showed Friday. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA AUG NEW YUAN LOANS CNY410.4B; M2 UP 28.53% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's banks extended CNY410.4 billion worth of new yuan loans in August, up from CNY355.9 billion in July and above economists' expectations, though they were still well below the first half's monthly average of CNY1.2 trillion. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA JULY INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT +6.8% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's July industrial output rose 6.8% from a year earlier, after a revised 8.2% increase in June, showed government data issued Friday. (published 0638 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA AUGUST FISCAL SURPLUS CNY50.04 BILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China recorded a fiscal surplus of CNY50.04 billion in August, maintaining a fiscal surplus for the fifth straight month, data issued by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday showed. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GOVERNMENT: THERE IS NO INFLATION IN CHINA NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China isn't facing inflation now, and higher prices reflect an increase in domestic demand, said Li Xiaochao, spokesman for the National Bureau of Statistics. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA GOVT: FIXED ASSET INVESTMENT TO SUPPORT 2H ECON GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's fixed asset investments will continue to support economic growth in the second half of this year, Li Xiaochao, spokesman for the National Bureau of Statistics, said Friday. (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DOLLAR FALLS BELOW KEY THB34 LEVEL, NOW AT THB33.96 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar fell below the key THB34.00 psychological level early Friday as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which had been propping up the greenback in recent weeks, has apparently pulled back from \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 PHILIPPINES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ' M3 MONEY SUPPLY +12.9% ON YR JULY VS +12.6% JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Broad money supply in the Philippines rose 12.9% from a year earlier in July, driven by an increase in net foreign assets, the Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas said Friday. (published 0546 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINES JULY BANK LENDING UP 8.7% ON YEAR VS +14.3% JUNE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philippine banks' outstanding loans in July rose 8.7% from a year earlier, compared with a 14.3% expansion in June, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0557 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RBNZ GOV SAYS HELPLESS AGAINST RISING NZ DLR TREND \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of New Zealand Governor Alan Bollard said Friday the continually rising local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is undesirable for the economy, but there's little the bank could do to halt the uptrend given the growing global thirst for more risk assets. (published 2309 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VIETNAM JAN-AUG BUDGET DEFICIT VND50.37 TRILLION - MINISTRY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam had a budget deficit of VND50.37 trillion in the first eight months of this year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0259 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PAKISTAN AUG TRADE DEFICIT NARROWS TO $1.04B VS $1.89B YR AGO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Pakistan's trade deficit narrowed in August to $1.04 billion from $1.89 billion a year earlier, the Federal Bureau of Statistics said Friday. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NZ'S AUG FOOD PRICES FALL, ANNUAL RATE SLIDES TO 17-MO LOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand's annual food price inflation eased sharply to a 17-month low in August, with grocery food and vegetable prices falling in the latest month, official figures released Friday showed. (published 2339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA APRA SEEKS ENHANCED LIQUIDITY REQUIREMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's prudential watchdog Friday proposed tougher liquidity risk management rules for the country's financial institutions as part of a broad review following the global financial crisis. (published 0205 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: AUSTRALIA CBA: GOVT DEBT GUARANTEE STILL VALUABLE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Offshore investors are increasingly warming to buying non-guaranteed debt from Australia's banks, though the government's term funding backstop still serves a vital role, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Treasurer Lyn Cobley said Friday. (published 0231 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =UPDATE: WYNN MACAU GETS LISTING OK FOR US$1B HK IPO -SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wynn Resorts Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has received Hong Kong regulatory approval to list its Macau casino \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the city in a US$1 billion initial public offering, people familiar with the situation said Friday. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: MYER REPORTS 15% PROFIT RISE, BEGINS IPO PROCESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In yet another bullish sign for Australia's retail sector, department store chain Myer Group Friday reported full year net profit rose 15% and began the process of becoming a public company in a float that could raise up to A$2.5 billion. (published 0337 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNITED GROUP WINS A$165M CONTRACT WITH BHP IRON ORE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it has won an A$165 million contract with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s iron ore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at Port Hedland, Western Australia. (published 0514 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PROTON RESTARTS TIE-UP TALKS WITH VOLKSWAGEN - EXEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia Proton Holdings Bhd., which called off talks on cooperation with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen\f28 \uc2 \f2  in November 2007, Friday said it has restarted discussions for a strategic tie-up with the German carmaker in a bid to be more competitive globally. (published 0347 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:WAREHOUSE FY NET PROFIT DOWN; UNDERLYING PROFIT UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand discount retailer The Warehouse Ltd. on Friday reported lower full-year net profit, but said underlying profit rose slightly despite tough trading conditions. (published 2306 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEXUS ENERGY: LONGTOM ASSET STAKE SALE TO AED WON'T PROCEED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oil and gas company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nexus Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that its planned sale of a 50% stake in the Longtom gas project to \f28 \uc2 \f2 AED Oil Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . won't go ahead due to delays in completion of the project. (published 0519 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ASAHI BREWERIES: NOT IN TALKS WITH ORANGINA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese beer maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asahi Breweries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it is not in talks with Orangina, denying an earlier media report that the European beverage maker is holding talks with both Suntory Holdings Ltd. and Asahi. (published 0014 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA OKS BANK OF CHINA TO BUY SHRS IN HENG AN STANDARD LIFE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The China Insurance Regulatory Commission said Thursday it approved \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of China Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s plan to buy shares in Heng An \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Life Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a 50-50 joint venture between U.K. insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Life PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Teda International. (published 2322 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:CHINA MOBILE CHMN:STILL IN TALKS WITH APPLE ON IPHONE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Mobile Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chairman Wang Jianzhou\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday the company is still in talks with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Apple Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . over selling iPhones in China. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ANSHAN IRON PRESIDENT: PLAN TO INCREASE OVERSEAS INVESTMENTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Anshan Iron & Steel Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , China's fifth-biggest steel producer by output, plans to increase its overseas investments, President Zhang Xiaogang said Thursday. "We are still talking with some potential targets at the moment, and we continue to look for overseas investment opportunities," Zhang told reporters on the sidelines of the World Economic Forum. (published 0152 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: VEDANTA MAKES NEW ASARCO BID, RAISING OFFER TO $2.5B \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vedanta Resources Plc\f28 \uc2 \f2  (VED.LN) is making a renewed bid to buy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Asarco LLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  out of bankruptcy, raising its offer to $2.56 billion after a judge last week recommended that Vedanta shouldn't get the Arizona mining company. (published 0000 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:BOFA MERRILL LYNCH NAMES BRILLE ASIA-PACIFIC PRES-MEMO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of America\f28 \uc2 \f2 Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2  has appointed Brian Brille, currently head of Americas Corporate & Investment Banking, as Asia-Pacific president, in one of the most senior transfers to the region by the Wall Street bank, according to a memo seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Friday. (published 0335 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW:THAI REGULATOR HOPES TO AUCTION 3G LICENSES BY YR-END \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's National Telecommunications Commission hopes to kick off the long-awaited auction of 2.1 gigahertz third-generation service licenses by the end of this year. (published 0238 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GODREJ GROUP CHMN: GODREJ PROPERTIES IPO IN NEXT 2-3 MONTHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Godrej Properties Ltd. - the real estate arm of India's Godrej Group - will launch an initial public offering in the next two to three months, the group's chairman said Friday. (published 0527 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OBEROI CONSTRUCTIONS PLANS IPO IN FIRST QTR OF 2010 - EXEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mumbai-based property developer Oberoi Constructions plans to launch an initial public offer to raise at least INR10 billion in the first quarter of the next calendar year, its managing director said Friday. (published 0651 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY HIGHER, CHEERED BY CHINESE DATA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares were mostly higher Friday, getting a boost from largely positive Chinese economic data. In Japan however, stocks were lower, weighed by the strong yen and as second-quarter economic growth was revised lower. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par =RECORD AUG LEAD OUTPUT DEFIES TALK OF CHINA PRODUCTION CUTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 11-09-09 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's lead output rose 26% on year in August, to a record 365,000 metric tons, along with record high volumes also posted for crude steel and copper, official data issued by the National Bureau of Statistics Friday showed. (published 0525 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE:OIL DATA:CHINA SEP CRUDE IMPORTS LIKELY STEADY ON MO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's crude oil imports in August slowed from July's all-time high, and September imports are unlikely to increase markedly even though a 240,000-barrel-a-day refinery has moved into full production. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA MAY GET WORLD'S FIRST FLOATING LNG PROJECT - ANALYST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia may accommodate the world's first large-scale floating liquefied natural gas plant, likely after 2015, amid a wider global increase in the technology's use, global energy consultancy \f28 \uc2 \f2 Poten & Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WARATAH MAY BUILD A$1.25B QUEENSLAND COAL POWER PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Waratah Coal Pty unit Galilee Power said Friday that it may build a A$1.25 billion, 900 Megawatt coal-fired power station in the Galilee Basin in Queensland state's central region. (published 0227 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA'S AUG COPPER,COPPER PDT IMPORTS SOAR ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China imported 325,098 metric tons of copper, copper alloy and semifinished products in August, down 20% from 406,612 tons in July, preliminary data provided Friday by the General Administration of Customs showed. (published 0413 GMT) [ 11-09-09 0707GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020090911e59b0009i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
