\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging debt-Asian debt spreads narrow on China hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 666 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2009\par 04:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2009 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, March 5 (Reuters) - Asian bond spreads narrowed on Thursday, as investors cheered China's plan to increase spending and implement other fiscal policies to support the world's third-largest economy.\par \par \uc2  China aims to achieve 8 percent growth this year, Premier Wen Jiabao told the National People's Congress. [ID:nPEK65604]\par \par \uc2  The Asia iTraxx investment-grade index <0#ITAIGMPBMK=> excluding Japan, a key measure of risk aversion, narrowed to 430/450 basis points from 440/470 on Wednesday, a Hong Kong-based trader said.\par \par \uc2   MSCI index of Asia-Pacific stocks outside Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> was up 0.5 percent at 0311 GMT.\par \par \uc2  The following were the major movers in cash bonds and credit default swaps (CDS):\par \par \uc2  -- CHINA'S five-year CDS <CHINA5UA=GFI> narrowed to 240/255 basis points from as much as 265 on Wednesday after Beijing announced economy-boosting measures.\par \par \uc2  -- SOUTH KOREA'S five-year CDS <KOREA5UA=GFI> narrowed to 420/450 basis points from 475/505, reflecting the return of risk appetite overnight.\par \par \uc2  Sentiment also improved as the won <KRW=> rebounded from 11-year lows after vice finance minister Hur Kyung-wook said the country's policy was to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "overshoots". [ID:nSEO92421]\par \par \uc2  -- \b \highlight22\uc2 PHILIPPINES\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' cash bonds gained ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's meeting on Thursday. Policy makers are seen cutting rates even after the inflation rate edged up to 7.3 percent in February from a year ago, the first increase since August and higher than January's 7.1 percent. [ID:nSP395982]\par \par \uc2  The country's 8.375 percent bonds maturing in 2019 <718286BE6=>, which were sold in January, were traded at 106.375/106.5 from 104.75/105.00.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, investors were awaiting for the outcome of Asia Aluminum's plan to buy back its debt. Asia Aluminum on Wednesday released a report detailing how much investors will get in the event the company is liquidated. [ID:nL4284026]\par \par \uc2  There were no trades recently on the company's bonds due to worries about its viability, traders said.\par \par \uc2  LATEST MAJOR RATINGS ACTIVITY IN ASIA (EXCLUDING JAPAN) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par >Fitch affirms China's ratings                [ID:nHKG102015]\par >Fitch affirms \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petronas\f28 \uc2 \f2 ' ratings                [ID:nWNA8094]\par >Moody's cuts CCT's ratings; outlook negative   [ID:nWLA8802]\par >Moody's cuts CPP to B3; outlook negative       [ID:nWLA8910]\par  FIVE-YEAR CREDIT DEFAULT SWAPS\par                             Bid/Ask spread\par                         Current         Week ago\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Dev Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2              524.65*           350/~\par  Hutchison                  ~/340             ~/320\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 PCCW-HKT\f28 \uc2 \f2                    525.00*           480/~\par  China                      ~/260           240/255\par  Indonesia                  650/700           600/~\par  Korea                      ~/460           430/440\par  Malaysia                   ~/320           290/305\par  Philippines                425/~             ~/480\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  ~ no bid or ask spread\par  For CDS prices double click on <GFICDS>\par  *midspread\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  ASIAN BENCHMARK DOLLAR BONDS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2                  Coupon     Maturity   Bid price   Bid\par spread\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  5-YEAR\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------\par  DBS Bank         7.13      15-May-11   104.88      280\par  Malaysia         7.50  