\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Central banks step in as Asia loses ground\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 713 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 07:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 27 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slid against the dollar on Monday as investors dumped assets amid heightened fears of a global downturn, forcing central banks in Indonesia and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The high-yielding Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> bore the brunt of the selling, briefly hitting as low as 10,800 per dollar but later steadied near 10,600 thanks to official \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupiah's drop of around 3.5 percent on Monday took its cumulative decline so far this year to 11 percent.\par \par \uc2 "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are selling the dollar at various levels from 10,300," said a trader in Jakarta.\par \par \uc2 A second trader said state banks were selling dollars at 10,600.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> lost 0.8 percent to 49.385 per dollar, its weakest since December 2006, despite dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to set a floor for the unit.\par \par \uc2 Some traders said they expected the peso to test the 49.50 level in the near term unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  more aggressively.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine stock index <.PSI> tumbled 10 percent on Monday, triggering an automatic suspension of trading.\par \par \uc2 The MSCI index of Asian stocks outside Japan <.MIAPJ0000PUS> fell for a fourth consecutive session, losing 4 percent as of 0520 GMT, marking its lowest since June 2004.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the South Korean won <KRW=> dropped as low as 1,447.9 per dollar as investors shrugged off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par move to slash its key interest rate by 75 basis points -- the\par biggest rate cut ever -- to calm the jittery market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the won, which has lost 35 percent against the dollar so far this year, would face further selling pressure in the near term amid the global market turmoil.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "However, we continue to believe that the won/dollar has overshot on the downside and expect the won to strengthen beyond the near term," they said in a note.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese yen climbed towards a 13-year peak against the dollar <JPY=> and an all-time high against the Australian dollar <AUDJPY=R>, as a slide in Tokyo shares overshadowed a G7 warning about excessive yen volatility.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Group of Seven big industrialised economices said on Monday that a rapid rise in the Japanese yen was bad for both markets and the economy and that it would watch developments accordingly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> was virtually flat at 6.8476 per dollar while the Hong Kong dollar <HKD=> eased slightly to 7.7535 per U.S. dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  injected HK$7.75 billion ($994 million) into the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bought U.S. dollars against the Hong Kong dollar last Thursday for the first time in nearly a year to stem a rise in the Hong Kong dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Hong Kong dollar is pegged to the U.S. dollar and can trade between 7.75 and 7.85 to the U.S. dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Markets in Singapore and Malaysia are closed for holiday. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0611 GMT \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.25          94.27       +1.09\par  Taiwan dlr      33.503         33.412       -0.27\par  Korean won     1441.80        1424.00       -1.23\par  Baht             34.73          34.65       -0.23\par  Peso             49.34          48.99       -0.71\par  Rupiah        10600.00       10225.00       -3.54\par  Rupee            50.12          49.96       -0.32\par  Yuan            6.8477         6.8433       -0.06\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen        93.25         111.33      +19.39\par  Sing dlr        1.5070         1.4382       -4.57\par  Taiwan dlr      33.503         32.443       -3.16\par  Korean won     1441.80         935.70      -35.10\par  Baht             34.73          33.68       -3.02\par  Peso             49.34          41.28      -16.34\par  Rupiah        10600.00        9390.00      -11.42\par  Rupee            50.12          39.41      -21.37\par  Ringgit         3.5785         3.3050       -7.64\par  Yuan            6.8477         7.3041       +6.67\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Editing by Jan Dahinten)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081030e4ar000ow\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
