ghlight\uc2 's banking development strategy department, was quoted as saying in a government monetary market report.\par \par \uc2 - - - -\par \par \uc2 BANGKOK - Thailand, the world's biggest rubber producer, plans to cut production by 700,000 tonnes in the six months starting from October to shore up prices, the Agriculture Ministry said.\par \par \uc2 "We will encourage farmers to tap less latex as we aim to cut rubber supply by 50 percent between October to March," Deputy Agriculture Minister Theerachai Saenkaew, who oversees rubber matters, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 - - - - (Compiled by Carl Bagh)\par \par \uc2 SOUTHEAST ASIA-HIGHLIGHTS 0900 GMT|LANGEN|Table|AFA|CSA|LBY|RWSA|RWS|REULB|GNS|RNA|G|RBN|SI|IF|PHD|RNP|DNP|PGE|SXNA   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020081027e4ar000wi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
