\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia rises in cautious trade as oil prices ease\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 752 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2008\par 05:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, May 28 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose on Wednesday as investors, encouraged by a drop in oil prices, cautiously moved to take profit on the dollar's steep gains in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2  Market talk that Malaysia may announce new measures to liberalise trade in the ringgit, additionally helped buoy the tightly managed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after recent losses.\par \par \uc2  The Thai baht <THB=TH> rose as far as 32.15 per dollar, up almost half of a percent from late Asian trade on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  "There have been some dollar selling this morning to take profit after the dollar gained too much yesterday," said a trader in Bangkok.\par \par \uc2  On Tuesday, the baht fell about 0.6 percent to its weakest level since May 16, in step with other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit by worries about the economic fallout from record high oil prices. The declines spurred authorities into action and central banks in South Korea, Indonesia and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  were seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to support their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  But a retreat in oil prices <CLc1> to below $127 per barrel on Wednesday from records above $135 hit last week offered markets some relief.\par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> hit a one-week high at 9,295 per dollar, up 0.5 percent from late Asian trade on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso <PHP=> also rose almost 0.5 percent to 43.55 per dollar.\par \par \uc2  "Oil prices came off overnight, which put some downward pressure on the dollar versus the peso," said a dealer in Manila.\par \par \uc2  A second trader said he expected the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to check on the peso's weakness for fear of fuelling inflation.\par \par \uc2  "They will come into the market if needed," he said.\par \par \uc2  The peso, has lost 5.5 percent against the dollar this year, trailing behind the South Korean won's 10 percent decline and the Indian rupee's 8 percent drop.\par \par \uc2  OUTLOOK UNCERTAIN\par \par \uc2  The Chinese yuan <CNY=CFXS> hit 6.9421 per dollar, up a fifth of a percent from Tuesday's close and bringing its gains so far this year to 5.2 percent.\par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> briefly rose to 30.493 to the U.S. dollar, cementing its position as the best performer in emerging Asia with gains of about 6.4 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2  However, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors remain wary after the recent sell-off.\par \par \uc2  "The near-term outlook will be uncertain and range-bound," said Thio Chin Loo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 BNP Paribas.\par \par \uc2  "A lot depends on commodity prices currently, if the prices head up, the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebound today may be temporary," she said.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the ringgit <MYR=> rose as far as 3.225 per dollar, up 0.4 percent from late Asian trade on Tuesday after three sessions of losses.\par \par \uc2  Some traders said renewed speculation that Malaysia would allow offshore trading in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  again underpinned the ringgit.\par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman declined to comment and investors hoped the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor's news conference on first quarter gross domestic product data would provide some clues whether any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy change was in fact on the cards.  \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0828 GMT \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.23         103.85       -0.36\par  Sing dlr        1.3621         1.3615       -0.04\par  Taiwan dlr      30.503         30.540       +0.12\par  Korean won     1035.70        1039.70       +0.39\par  Baht             32.24          32.30       +0.19\par  Peso             43.69          43.75       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9295.00        9345.00       +0.54\par  Rupee            42.81          42.96       +0.35\par  Ringgit         3.2430         3.2460       +0.09\par  Yuan            6.9441         6.9559       +0.17\par  Change so far in 2008\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       104.23         111.33       +6.81\par  Sing dlr        1.3621         1.4382       +5.59\par  Taiwan dlr      30.503         32.443       +6.36\par  Korean won     1035.70         935.70       -9.66\par  Baht             32.24          33.68       +4.47\par  Peso             43.69          41.28       -5.52\par  Rupiah         9295.00        9390.00       +1.02\par  Rupee            42.81          39.41       -7.94\par  Ringgit         3.2430         3.3050       +1.91\par  Yuan            6.9441         7.3041       +5.18\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2  (Editing by Tomasz Janowski)\par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|D|E|RBN|IF|PHD|SI|Z|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080531e45s0001x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picsc