\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Arroyo: No Direct  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt  \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 07:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MANILA (Dow Jones)--Despite complaints from exporters that a stronger peso is hurting their competitiveness, Philippine President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo on Thursday dismissed the possibility of any direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Instead, Arroyo said in a nationwide televised address that the government will provide assistance to exporters to cut their costs and maintain their competitiveness.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which makes exchange rate policy doesn't agree to (direct) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Arroyo. "So our \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be in other ways to reduce the cost of exporters." [ 23-03-06 0632GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 She said government financial institutions will help provide cheap financing to exporters, while government offices will have to streamline export regulations.  \par \par \uc2 "The appreciation of the peso helps the majority, but we must still protect our exporters," Arroyo said.  \par \par \uc2 Improved revenue and a narrower budget deficit have boosted the peso's value against the dollar in recent months. Since the end of September - when Arroyo quashed an effort to impeach her - the peso has risen against the dollar by around 10%, with the greenback falling from PHP56.01 to a 3 1/2-year low of PHP50.88 early this month.  \par \par \uc2 At midday Thursday, the dollar was at PHP51.16.  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine Exporters Confederation has publicly urged the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust economic policies to balance the interests of other segments of the economy with those of exporters and of the families of 8 million overseas workers who send dollar remittances home.  \par \par \uc2 -By Cris Larano, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-848-5051; cris.larano@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Michael Kitchen [ 23-03-06 0656GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060323e23n0007t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
