\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk: Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In Mkt Only If Needed  \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2006\par 09:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MANILA (Dow Jones)--The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday it will continue to allow market forces to determine the peso-dollar exchange rate, but it is ready to provide liquidity to smooth extreme volatility in the spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas Governor Amando Tetangco told a government-sponsored investor briefing that there is "scope for occasional official action in cases where extreme movements in the peso threaten the inflation target."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  projects inflation next year will ease to 4.4%-5.8%, from a projected 7.5%-8.3% range for this year. The official target is average inflation of 4%-5% for both years.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders suspect that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying U.S. dollars in recent weeks to boost its reserves. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had refused to comment.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the dollar to average PHP55-PHP57 this year after an average of PHP55.09 in 2005. However, the dollar fell to a three-year low of PHP51.57 Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Filipinos in higher paying jobs overseas are expected to boost remittances to $11.8 billion this year, 10% more than the estimated $10.7 billion in 2005. In the 11 months to November 2005, remittances rose 27% over the same period the year before, to $9.7 billion.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is forecasting gross international reserves for 2006 to be between $18 billion and $18.6 billion, compared with an end-2005 level of $18.495 billion. At the end of January, reserves were already at an all-time high of $20.504 billion due to fresh government borrowing and gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overseas investments.  \par \par \uc2 -By Ditas Lopez and Cris Larano, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-848-5051; cris.larano@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 07-02-06 0804GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060207e227000em\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
