\par\par \b \uc2 Philippine Ctrl Bk Says Not  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt  \b0\par\par\uc2 423 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2005\par 05:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 MANILA (Dow Jones)--The Bangko Sentral ng Pilipinas (\b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) on Tuesday said it's not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to boost the peso against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "No \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Bangko Sentral acting governor Amando Tetangco said when asked if the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  injected liquidity in the Philippine Dealing System to help curb the dollar's rise against the peso.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar opened at PHP55.65 Tuesday, up sharply from its previous close of PHP55.51. The U.S. unit quickly climbed to an intraday high of PHP55.68 before dropping to an intraday low of PHP55.49.  \par \par \uc2 "It's just trading within range. The opening could have been a knee jerk reaction to the statement last night," said Tetangco, referring to President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo's nationwide address late Monday on the alleged wiretapped recordings between her and an election official discussing plans to rig last year's presidential race.  \par \par \uc2 In her address, Arroyo admitted talking to an election official during last year's presidential race, but denied rigging the election. [ 28-06-05 0321GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Tetangco also noted that the thin corporate demand may have contributed to the recovery of the peso against the dollar in morning trading.  \par \par \uc2 Asked if he expected continued fallout in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from Arroyo's speech, Tetangco said that based on the peso's performance so far, he didn't see that happening.  \par \par \uc2 In late morning trading, the dollar was averaging PHP55.552 with volume of trades at $131 million. The bids ranged between PHP55.545-PHP55.58.  \par \par \uc2 In a nationwide address late Monday, Arroyo apologized for phoning an election official while votes were still being counted after last year's closely fought presidential vote. But she but said the call hadn't influenced the outcome and she wouldn't step down.  \par \par \uc2 Arroyo's opponents have used a recording of the conversation - the source of which is unclear - to accuse her of attempting to rig the election. Several thousand demonstrators marched in Manila on Friday demanding that Arroyo resign over the controversy.  \par \par \uc2 During the nationally televised address, Arroyo broke weeks of silence to apologize for phoning the election official. She said long delays in the counting of the vote and concerns about electoral fraud prompted her to make the call, which, though not illegal, is widely perceived as inappropriate.  \par \par \uc2 -By Micheline R. Millar, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288; micheline.millar@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Costas Paris and Paul Baylis [ 28-06-05 0418GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020050628e16s0000a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
