\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Peso falls, baht steady in light trade.  \b0\par\par\uc2 629 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2004\par 08:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The Philippine peso eased on\par Thursday while the Thai baht moved little, with most Asian\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets shut for the Lunar New Year holidays.\par  \par     Financial markets in Hong Kong, South Korea, Singapore,\par Indonesia, Malaysia and Taiwan were closed on Thursday.\par     Markets will reopen in Indonesia on Friday. Singapore,\par South Korea, Hong Kong and Malaysia will reopen on Monday and\par Taiwan will resume trade on Tuesday.\par     The peso fell by about a quarter percent to 55.68 per\par dollar, from Wednesday's local close of 55.56.\par     Dealers in Manila said the peso fell as local companies\par bought U.S. dollars in the absence of any significant inflows\par of that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The baht was glued to a tight range of 39.0 to 39.05 per\par dollar, as only a few dealing rooms were active in Bangkok.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "There were no offshore names and even our local customers\par were out of the market because of the holiday," said a dealer\par at a local bank in Bangkok.\par     The dealer said the baht might stick to a narrow range\par around the 39 per dollar level on Friday as well, but some\par action was likely next week.\par     "There is interest, both local and offshore, to push the\par baht higher," the dealer said.\par     "But players will be careful as they have already seen the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market this week," he said, adding that the\par Bank of Thailand had helped pull the baht to 39.08 on Tuesday.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also suspected in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  where\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 dealers said the Philippines \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had bought pesos to  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 pull the troubled \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  off two-month lows it had hit on  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tuesday.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     The peso, Asia's worst performer in 2003, is expected to\par suffer more losses ahead of presidential elections in May.\par     A three-month election campaign in the Philippines will\par formally start on February 8.\par     Many analysts fear that electioneering could weaken the\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 budget and prompt foreign lenders to ask for much higher  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 interest rates on loans to the country, Asia's most active  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 borrower of dollars outside of Japan.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     But for the next few weeks, dealers said, the U.S. dollar's\par global decline might help put a floor under the peso.\par     The peso touched an all-time low of 55.85 per dollar in\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November last year, and many dealers expect that level to be  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 tested again as the import season in the second quarter kicks  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 in.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     In contrast, traders are bullish on the baht, which\par strengthened by about nine percent against the dollar in 2003.\par     Many analysts expect the baht to strengthen towards 38 per\par dollar and beyond in 2004, despite several capital controls\par imposed by Thailand last year to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's rise.\par     They expect authorities in Thailand, one of Asia's fastest\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 growing economies, to lower their resistance to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 gains.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Change on the day 0700 GMT   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.73         107.14       +0.38\par  Sing dlr        1.7014         1.7014        0.00\par  Taiwan dlr      33.719         33.719        0.00\par  Korean won     1188.00        1188.00        0.00\par  Baht             39.01          38.99       -0.05\par  Peso             55.65          55.56       -0.16\par  Rupiah         8398.00        8398.00        0.00\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       106.73         107.31       +0.54\par  Sing dlr        1.7014         1.6978       -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      33.719         33.978       +0.77\par  Korean won     1188.00        1192.00       +0.34\par  Baht             39.01          39.59       +1.47\par  Peso             55.65          55.49       -0.29\par  Rupiah         8398.00        8410.00       +0.14.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040122e01m002vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
