\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Manila c.bank says can provide  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  liquidity. \b0\par\par\uc2 375 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2003\par 10:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  MANILA, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it stood ready to pump liquidity into the financial system as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged to fresh 31-month lows. \par \par \uc2  "We will provide liquidity as necessary. That policy has never changed," Deputy Governor Amando Tetangco told reporters when asked whether the bank would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the peso's slide. \par \par \uc2  "Our policy continues to be the same - to essentially let market forces determine the exchange rate." \par \par \uc2  The peso  was quoted at 55.40/44 on Monday afternoon, perilously close to its all-time low of 55.75 in January 2001 when Joseph Estrada was ousted from the presidency in an army-backed popular revolt. \par \par \uc2  Jitters over a failed uprising by renegade soldiers on July 27, a court-ordered suspension of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor and money laundering accusations against the husband of President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo have combined with seasonal dollar demand to put the peso under heavy pressure in the past two weeks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have denied it has been injecting funds into the market, although traders say the bank has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a number of occasions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a limited ability to support the peso as its gross foreign reserves stand at just over $16 billion. \par \par \uc2  The continued slide in the peso has revived market talk the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may consider hiking its overnight rates or making other monetary policy moves. \par \par \uc2  The bank's monthly policy meeting will be held on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  To deter speculation in the peso before the Iraq war, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hiked the reserve requirement for commercial banks to eight percent from seven percent on March 20, squeezing an estimated $224 million in liquidity from the financial system. \par \par \uc2  Governor Rafael Buenaventura said recently the peso's weakness was a temporary phenomenon and that hiking overnight rates not an appropriate response. \par \par \uc2  In July, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market by cutting policy rates for the first time since March 2002. \par \par \uc2  The cut of 25 basis points took the overnight borrowing rate to 6.75 percent and the lending rate to 9.0 percent - their lowest levels in more than 11 years. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030825dz8p00h4q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
