\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Focus shifts to stocks from security. \b0\par\par\uc2 734 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2003\par 05:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Vidya Ranganathan\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 18 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were shored\par up on Monday morning by rising stock markets in the region and\par some relief after the weekend passed without any militant\par attacks.\par     The Korean won                   was knocking at a key\par resistance at 1,175 and the Taiwan dollar  reached its\par strongest in a month. Korean stocks  rose to an\par eight-month high and Taiwan's shares  were furthering\par gains after hitting 14-month highs last week.\par     Indonesia's markets were closed for the National Day\par holiday, but in thin offshore deals the rupiah  was\par quoted higher. Markets had sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  last week on\par security fears after the capture of Muslim militant Hambali in\par Thailand and the bombing of a Jakarta hotel earlier this month.\par     The Singapore dollar        was steady, but sentiment on\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was bullish after some proposed changes to the\par city-state's pension systems.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore's Straits Times Index        hit a 13-month high,\par resuming an rally that was broken on Friday. Prime Minister Goh\par Chok Tong said on Sunday that workers should expect\par contributions to the national pension fund to drop to 30\par percent from the current 36 percent.\par     "The strengthening of the Sing dollar does not surprise me.\par It has been too weak, trading close to the mid-point of the\par basket for the last few months," said Peter Redward, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par strategist with Deutsche bank.\par     The Singapore dollar is managed in an undisclosed\par trade-weighted band, and analysts estimate it is allowed to\par move around 1.5 to 2.0 percent on either side of a mid-point.\par     "We believe that based on the magnitude of the current\par account surplus, which is running close to 27 percent of GDP,\par the relatively strong performance of the Straits Times Index\par versus the S&P 500  and the low interest rate\par differential, the Sing should be performing better and trading\par close to the top end of the band," Redward said.\par  \par     JP Morgan calculated the mid-point of their U.S.\par dollar/Singapore dollar band to be 1.7620.\par     "We would not recommend going long U.S. dollars until spot\par falls below 1.7450," JP Morgan said in a report.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     Elsewhere, Tokyo's Nikkei Average         tested 10,000 but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the yen inched lower against the U.S. dollar, which firmed on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations of improved economic growth and as the impact of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the major power outages in northeastern United States receded.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the weakening yen  stopped\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Thai baht  from revisiting Friday's highs of 41.58\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar, even though the Bank of Thailand said on Friday it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was not worried about the strong baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There was no \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reported in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par either, as the peso  settled in a narrow band on the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lower side of 55 per dollar in thin volumes.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Redward said the Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to step in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and prevent the won firming past 1,175, particularly with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won gaining against the yen too .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     "The Bank of Korea will be more aggressive in defending\par dollar-Korea," Redward said.\par     "Dollar-Taiwan has a little more downside. The CBC's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) policy is slightly different from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BOK's and its approach is to allow the Taiwan dollar to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gradually appreciate over a period of time," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0330 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.36       118.96         -0.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7478       1.7482         +0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.335       34.358         +0.07\par  Korean won   1175.20      1178.00         +0.24\par  Baht           41.61        41.63         +0.05\par  Peso           55.04        55.06         +0.04\par  Rupiah       8496.00      8532.00         +0.42\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     119.36       118.74         -0.52\par  Sing dlr      1.7478       1.7341         -0.78\par  Taiwan dlr    34.335       34.753         +1.22\par  Korean won   1175.20      1185.80         +0.90\par  Baht           41.61        43.08         +3.53\par  Peso           55.04        53.38         -3.02\par  Rupiah       8496.00      8940