\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Speculation steps up pressure. \b0\par\par\uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2002\par 11:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Oct 11 (Reuters) - Speculative buying of dollars in the forward markets on Friday piled pressure on Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  already beset by worries over growth, foreign investor aversion and a dithering yen. \par \par \uc2  Many regionals hit multi-month lows, although \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped take the heat off the sliding Taiwan dollar and Korean won. \par \par \uc2  A rally on Wall Street gave the dollar some early bounce, as did adjustments ahead of market holidays in the United States, Hong Kong and Japan on Monday. \par \par \uc2  But profit-booking dollar sales helped regionals off their lows, even though the yen hit four-month lows against the dollar after the Bank of Japan left monetary policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  "Understandably there is some position-squaring as people close out before the weekend," said Tim Fallowfield, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at ING Barings. \par \par \uc2  And speculative buying had increased in recent sessions, taking Asian regionals further down, he said. \par \par \uc2  "For a month now, we've been seeing domestic oil companies buying dollars aggressively and foreign players take investments out. And now, speculative money too has come into these \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," Fallowfield said. \par \par \uc2  The speculation was largely in the non-deliverable forwards. Longer-tenor forwards on the Taiwan dollar reversed to positive on the pressure, while in Thailand one-year swap points in the offshore market surged to 74/77 points from a low of 50 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the heaviest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen in the Taiwan dollar, which hit an intra-day low of 35.22 while catching up with losses in other regionals after a holiday on Thursday, amid weak stocks and foreigners selling equities. \par \par \uc2  "In the near-term, the risks are still for the pair (US dollar-Taiwan dollar) to go up but the pair has to break 35.30, which is expected to be another strong resistance, in order to move further higher," Bank of America said in its market note. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  support for the Philippine peso was less obvious. Though it came marginally off an intra-day low of 52.855, traders merely suspected some covert \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Morgan Stanley's downgrade of \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' external debt to underperform, announced on Friday, could have played a part in driving the peso down, traders said. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS HIT THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  A two percent fall in Thai stocks depressed the Thai baht , leading markets to ignore recent upgrades in economists' growth outlooks and rating agency Fitch's upgrading of its outlook for Thailand to positive this week. \par \par \uc2  It fell to a six-month low of 43.88 in morning deals, and was unable to move too far away from there through afternoon trade. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar hit an early low of 1.7951, a level last seen four months ago, before recovering slightly on suspected unwinding of some option contracts and spent the day in a dull range \par \par \uc2  Thursday's startling drop in Singapore's third quarter GDP started the push against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and raised concerns that other regional economies may show similar deceleration. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won was volatile, hitting a five-month low of 1,266 per dollar before a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement expressing worry at the slide helped it recoup some of its losses. \par \par \uc2  The weak yen weighed on the won, although it was supported by speculation that the inflows from a sale of a $230 million stake in state-run Korea Tobacco and Ginseng Corp through global depositary receipts had hit the market. \par \par \uc2  "Sentiment on won is likely to remain negative in the near-term, given the risk aversion in the financial markets. The dollar could test 1280 level in the near-term," Bank of America said, recommending long dollar positions against the won. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0900 GMT Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Japan yen     124.08       123.35         -0.59\par   Sing dlr      1.7929       1.7914         -0.08\par   Taiwan dlr    35.157       35.111         -0.13\par   Korean won   1258.80      1257.50         -0.10\par   Baht           43.85        43.75         -0.23\par   Peso           52.71        52.67         -0.08\par   Rupiah       9007.00      9005.00         -0.02\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par   Japan yen     124.08       131.24         +5.77\par   Sing dlr      1.7929       1.8515         +3.27\par   Taiwan dlr    35.157       34.986         -0.49\par   Korean won   1258.80      1277.00         +1.45\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Baht 43.85 44.16 +0.71 Peso 52.71 51.50 -2.30 Rupiah 9007.00 10350.00\par +14.91.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021011dyab00jah\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
