\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP:Philippines In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Swap Pact Talks With China, Korea \b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 09:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- The Philippines is in talks with South Korea and China for bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap arrangements to bolster its dollar buffer against future financial market shocks, a senior Manila monetary official said Monday. \par \par \uc2  The official, who asked not to be named, said the pact with South Korea should be completed by the end of May. \par \par \uc2  "This is an additional arsenal that we can depend on but we are still finalizing the amounts," said the official, adding that swap lines would likely be under $3 billion each. \par \par \uc2  Last July, the Philippines concluded a bilateral swap agreement with Japan, giving it a potential $3 billion credit line to defend the peso if it comes under speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  The swap arrangements are part of a broader effort by some Southeast Asian nations to forge similar pacts with the region's strongest economies: Japan, South Korea and China. \par \par \uc2  Two years ago at a meeting in Chiang Mai, Thailand, the 10-member Association of Southeast Asian Nations, or Asean, launched the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -protection initiative to strengthen economic and financial cooperation in the region. \par \par \uc2  Kwon Tae-shin, director general of the international finance bureau at South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy, said talks have been ongoing with the Philippines for five or six months regarding the swap arrangement. \par \par \uc2  The monetary official said talks with China for a timetable to open negotiations are underway. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministers from Asean and the so-called "plus three" group are scheduled to hold a meeting next weekend in Myanmar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the swap arrangement shouldn't impact on South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market or economy. \par \par \uc2  "Frankly, there will be no impact on the current economy," said Oh Suktae, an economist at Citibank in Seoul. "The economic relationship with the Philippines isn't that deep. We cannot say that it is small, but it is not significantly big enough to effect the overall picture." \par \par \uc2  Oh added that the move could be a step toward bigger agreements with all Asian nations, however. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Defending The Peso If Renewed Attack\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the Philippines, swap lines should enable the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par defend the peso without depleting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves that are already\par among the lowest in the region. Gross international reserves totaled\par $16.3 billion at the end of February, compared with double that in\par Malaysia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Under the swap scheme with Japan, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may borrow dollars\par in exchange for pesos as collateral to meet unusually heavy demand for\par dollars on the peso market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The monetary official noted that before funds can be disbursed from\par the facility approval must be given by the International Monetary Fund\par in the form of a "seal of good housekeeping." As matters stand, the\par Philippines doesn't have a loan program with the IMF, but economic and\par financial targets are periodically reviewed by the Fund in a monitoring\par program.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Much further down the road, bilateral agreements may eventually be\par signed between the Philippines and other Asean countries, such as\par Malaysia, the official said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The swap agreement with Japan hasn't been utilized, with the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  using its existing reserves in recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to quell\par speculative pressure on the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After spending around $2 billion in an ultimately futile defense of\par the peso shortly after the outbreak of Asia's 1997-1998 financial\par crisis, Manila's monetary managers have generally used \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a\par last resort.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even so, expanding the swap lines to cover commitments from South\par Korea and China are important defenses against any future speculative\par attacks on the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the past several months, however, improving economic, financial\par and political fundamentals have kept the peso on an even keel against\par the dollar of between PHP51 to PHP52.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar averaged PHP51.139 in early trading Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amethyst Ma and Laura Pohl, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288;\par alastair.mcindoe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020325dy3p000f8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
