\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP: Philippines, South Korea Plan  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Swap Pact \b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 07:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- The Philippines is in talks with South Korea for a bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap arrangement to bolster Manila's dollar buffer against future financial market shocks. \par \par \uc2  An agreement should be reached before the end of May, said Kwon Tae-shin, director general of the international finance bureau at South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Economy. \par \par \uc2  Kwon told Dow Jones Newswires Thursday that the amount of the swap line hasn't been finalized yet, but sources quoted in a Manila newspaper said it may be around $2 billion. \par \par \uc2  The same newspaper, BusinessWorld, said the Philippines is also in talks with finance and monetary officials in China to secure a similar arrangement of up to $1 billion. \par \par \uc2  Last July, the Philippines concluded a bilateral swap agreement with Japan, giving it a potential $3 billion credit line to defend the peso if it comes under speculative attack. \par \par \uc2  The swap arrangements are part of a broader effort by some Southeast Asian nations to forge similar pacts with the region's strongest economies: Japan, South Korea and China. \par \par \uc2  Two years ago at a meeting in Chiang Mai, Thailand, the 10-member Association of Southeast Asian Nations, or Asean, launched the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -protection initiative to strengthen economic and financial cooperation in the region. \par \par \uc2  Kwon said Seoul and Manila have been in talks for five or six months regarding the swap arrangement. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Finance Ministers Meeting In Myanmar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance ministers from Asean and the so-called "plus three" group are\par scheduled to hold a meeting next weekend in Myanmar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the swap arrangement shouldn't impact on South Korea's\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market or economy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Frankly, there will be no impact on the current economy," said Oh\par Suktae, an economist at Citibank in Seoul. "The economic relationship\par with the Philippines isn't that deep. We cannot say that it is small,\par but it is not significantly big enough to effect the overall picture."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Oh added that the move could be a step toward bigger agreements with\par all Asian nations, however.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the Philippines, swap lines should enable the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par defend the peso without depleting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves that are already\par among the lowest in the region. Gross international reserves totaled\par $16.3 billion at the end of February, compared with double that in\par Malaysia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Under the swap scheme with Japan, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may borrow dollars\par in exchange for pesos as collateral to meet unusually heavy demand for\par dollars on the peso market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bulk of funds under existing bilateral swap arrangements may only\par be released by an official loan program approved by the International\par Monetary Fund. In extreme cases, however, up to 10% of a credit line may\par be tapped.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The swap agreement with Japan hasn't been utilized, with the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Philippines\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  using its existing reserves in recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to quell\par speculative pressure on the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par After spending around $2 billion in an ultimately futile defense of\par the peso shortly after the outbreak of Asia's 1997-1998 financial\par crisis, Manila's monetary managers have generally used \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a\par last resort.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Even so, expanding the swap lines to cover commitments from South\par Korea and China are important defenses against any future speculative\par attacks on the peso.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For the past several months, however, improving economic, financial\par and political fundamentals have kept the peso on an even keel against\par the dollar of between PHP51 to PHP52.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar averaged PHP51.139 in morning trading Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Alastair McIndoe and Laura Pohl, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 632-885-0288; alastair.mcindoe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020325dy3p000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
