\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mixed bag, yen and c.banks watched. \b0\par\par\uc2 839 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2001\par 11:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Sept 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a \par \par \uc2  mixed bag in late trade on Wednesday with the market \par \par \uc2  wrongfooted by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japan and by local central \par \par \uc2  banks. \par \par \uc2      The regionals had followed the yen firmer early but turned \par \par \uc2  tail when the Bank of Japan stepped in to sell yen on at least \par \par \uc2  two occasions lifting the dollar away from the 117.00 level. \par \par \uc2      This is the second time this week the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  stem the yen's rapid appreciation. However, the action was only \par \par \uc2  a partial success with the dollar unable even to hold 118.00 \par \par \uc2  yen. \par \par \uc2      The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also had to weather \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of their own. \par \par \uc2      In the \b \highlight22\uc2 Philippines\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was rumoured to have \par \par \uc2  aggressively sold U.S. dollars to countered losses in the peso \par \par \uc2  caused by demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to settle maturing deals \par \par \uc2  in the non-deliverable forward market. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also offered dollars to curb \par \par \uc2  the rupiah's slide which resulted from active dollar demand \par \par \uc2  from local banks and companies. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar drifted below the key 1.7400 market after \par \par \uc2  the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted dealers to mark the dollar higher \par \par \uc2  and some players to cover short positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore so far, but there was talk the \par \par \uc2  MAS has left dollar buying orders open at 1.7340. \par \par \uc2  Charts show the Sing dollar is trading around its 14-day \par \par \uc2  moving average of 1.7419, and also that there is a gap up to \par \par \uc2  1.7500 left after last week's plane attacks which the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  was likely to fill sooner or later. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht was a touch firmer at 44.15, but still locked in a \par \par \uc2  tight range of 44.10-44.24 after gains inspired by foreign \par \par \uc2  stock buying were countered by exporter dollar offers above \par \par \uc2  44.20. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors had been net buyers of Thai stocks since \par \par \uc2  last Thursday. \par \par \uc2      On the macro front, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief economist Atchana \par \par \uc2  Waiquamdee said the volatile world political and economic \par \par \uc2  situation may leave Thailand with lower than expected economic \par \par \uc2  growth in 2002. \par \par \uc2  "If the world situation persists and worsens, we could see \par \par \uc2  a technical recession in 2002, when the economy contracts for \par \par \uc2  two consecutive quarters," she said. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah briefly dropped below 9,700 for the first time \par \par \uc2  since August 2 on the back of aggressive dollar buying from \par \par \uc2  local banks and companies, including one oil importer. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crawled off its lows after Bank Indonesia \par \par \uc2  sold the dollar at around 9,700 and some local firms took \par \par \uc2  profits on the dollar. \par \par \uc2  BI had said earlier on Wednesday that it was considering \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the \par \par \uc2  rupiah. But dealers said the amount of its dollar sales was \par \par \uc2  small. \par \par \uc2  Deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Miranda Goeltrom also told \par \par \uc2  Reuters there was a "likelihood" that benchmark SBI interest \par \par \uc2  rates would fall further. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso closed lower at 51.40 to the dollar in the onshore \par \par \uc2  market against 51.370 on Tuesday despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Market players needed the U.S. dollar to settle their deals \par \par \uc2  in the NDF market. \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Manila said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar sales accounted \par \par \uc2  for almost half of the total market turnover on Wednesday which \par \par \uc2  was around $73.50 million. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  later said \par \par \uc2  they had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said separately \par \par \uc2  he was quite comfortable with the current level of the peso. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won ended higher against the dollar as a rate cut by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the yen's resilience provided support for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won closed at 1,296.50 to the dollar against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's close of 1,296.9.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday cut its target for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term call rate by 50 basis points to 4.00 percent,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par joining a global monetary easing to minimise impacts from U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attacks on the world economy.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0912 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     117.42       117.90         +0.41\par  Sing dlr      1.7410       1.7376         -0.20\par  Taiwan dlr    34.572       34.575         +0.01\par  Korean won   1295.50      1297.00         +0.12\par  Baht           44.16        44.20         +0.09\par  Peso           51.38        51.37         -0.02\par  Rupiah       9590.00      9540.00         -0.52\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     117.42       114.45         -2.53\par  Sing dlr      1.7410       1.7365         -0.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.572       32.900         -4.84\par  Korean won   1295.50      1277.00         -1.43\par  Baht           44.16        43.70         -1.04\par  Peso           51.38        50.75         -1.23\par  Rupiah       9590.00      9470