\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Philippines \highlight\uc2  Buenaventura: Ctrl Bk Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2001\par 05:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  MANILA -(Dow Jones)- The Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the spot market to support the peso so far Friday, but is willing to sell dollars to ease a liquidity crunch if necessary. \par \par \uc2  "We're watching the market," Buenaventura told reporters, adding that the bank will provide liquidity if necessary. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some traders believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars to stop the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  breaching its intraday high of PHP53.220.\par - - 13/07/01 03-46G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We will provide liquidity if there's a crunch, but so far we haven't\par seen (demand for dollars) in large proportions," Buenaventura said.\par "Sometimes there are just imbalances."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Buenaventura's comments suggest the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief believes\par speculation is at least partly responsible for the pressure on the peso\par this week and referred to some participants "playing around" with the\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I'm a little bit annoyed because it affects a lot of people," he\par said. "We're trying to discourage that."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso is under pressure from the malaise afflicting emerging-market\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  due partly to the financial crisis in Argentina, as well as\par from domestic factors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At the noon recess, the dollar averaged PHP53.190, up from PHP53.080\par at the previous close.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar rose to PHP53.40 Thursday, its highest level since\par President Gloria Macapagal Arroyo came to power Jan. 20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Amethyst Ma, Dow Jones Newswires; 632-885-0288;\par amethyst.ma@dowjones.com\par -0- 13/07/01 04-12G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010713dx7d0006u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
